(Preah Sihanouk): The Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration has decided to block Sihanoukville for 14 days to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 after the disease has been on the rise in recent days.
The closure runs from April 23 to May 6. During the blockade, the provincial administration prohibits travel and evacuation, except in rare cases. Businesses are also banned, except for businesses that are essential to people's daily lives, such as health services and food supplies.
In order to ensure the effective implementation of this, the force of the Sihanoukville Provincial Police under the direct command of Major General Chuon Narin, the Provincial Police Commissioner, in cooperation with the relevant authorities, also set up barricades at all blocked targets. .
