Samdech Techo Hun Sen is leading a delegation on a special Cambodian flight to Jakarta to attend the Special ASEAN Summit (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the afternoon of April 23, 2021 That Samdech is leading a government delegation on a special Cambodian flight to Jakarta to attend the special ASEAN Summit on April 24.
Through his official Facebook page, the Prime Minister stated: "At the moment, I am leading a high-level Royal Government delegation on a special Cambodian flight to Jakarta, Republic of Indonesia to attend a special ASEAN Summit. "Most ASEAN leaders will arrive in Jakarta this afternoon."
Samdech stated that according to the program scheduled for April 24, 2021, Samdech will attend informal meetings of ASEAN leaders and some meetings with other ASEAN leaders. After a full day of meetings, Samdech will return to Cambodia on the evening of April 24.
Samdech continued that upon arrival in Cambodia, Samdech and the delegation will provide samples to check 19 Kovid at Phnom Penh International Airport to ensure the safety and health of all.
Samdech thanked the authorities and the armed forces for taking care to implement Kovid 19 protection measures to protect the lives of the people as well as the timely supply of food to the people.
The Ministry of Health added the second vaccination site for Sino-Vaccine in Toul Kork district during the closure of Phnom Penh and Takhmao
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health, through the National Commission for the Kovid 19 Vaccination, has decided to add two Sino-Vaccine sites in Toul Kork district during the implementation of blockade measures in Phnom Penh and Takhmao City, Kandal Province. This is according to the announcement received by Fresh News on the afternoon of April 23, 2021.
In order to expedite the vaccination of Sino-Vaccine II, the Commission decided to add one more vaccination site in Tuol Kork district, at the National Children's Hospital, which started the second vaccination of Sino-Vaccine on 24 to 30 April 2021.
Individuals who have been vaccinated against the second dose of Sino-Vaccine should go to the above location to be vaccinated without having to cross the border.
At the same time, the National Committee for the Kovid 19 Vaccination has requested the local authorities to list the individuals who have been vaccinated for the second dose and who are currently being vaccinated in the Red Zone in Phnom Penh. Prepare a second dose for them.
Earlier this week, Thai Prime Minister Prayuth Chan-o-cha decided not to attend the ASEAN Summit in Jakarta, Indonesia, because he wanted to stay in Thailand to manage the worsening situation of COVID-19. . As for the COVID-19 vaccination campaign, as of Friday, Thailand had given a total of 964,825 doses of the vaccine to the population.
General Knowledge: Oceania in the Colonial Period (Part 14)
(Oceania): Apart from the Indian subcontinent and Southeast Asia, Oceania was also a fierce battleground for colonies. During the conquest of this colony, the Europeans also settled in large numbers in Oceania, and they also declared independence from the European powers, forming many small and large countries to this day.
Of course, the Portuguese did not go deep into Oceania, only the archipelago of Timor-Leste, because Portugal and Spain followed the Treaty of Tordesillas, which divided one world in half. The border is in East Timor.
During World War II, Japan placed many colonies in the archipelago of Oceania, the former territory of the Western powers, by force.
(Kampong Speu): Major General Sam Samoun, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Speu, this morning, April 23, 2021, confirmed that the police force of Kampong Speu Provincial Police has cracked down on two cases of human trafficking from closed areas in Phnom Penh. The case involved the arrest of four Cambodians transporting people and the arrest of 34 foreigners (16 Indonesians and 18 Chinese).
For the first case, on April 20, 2021, his police force arrested 16 Indonesians, including four women and two Cambodians, according to Lt. Gen. Sam Samoun. He was a taxi driver who was stopped at Udong Market, Veang Chas Commune, Udong District. After questioning, they admitted that they intended to travel to Poipet, Banteay Meanchey province.
According to the General Commissioner for the 16 Indonesians, each was fined 1.2 million riels and sent to the General Department of Immigration for further action. Separately, the two Cambodians, who are taxi drivers, have been sent to court and have been detained.
For the second case, on the morning of April 23, 2021, his police force continued to crack down on the transportation of 18 Chinese nationals at the same Udong market while traveling to Battambang province. Two Cambodians were also arrested.
The response to a report by Reporters Without Borders by a spokesman for the Cambodian Human Rights Commission came after the organization ranked Cambodia 144th out of 180 countries for freedom of the press and expression.
First, this report looks at only one aspect of the enforcement of the law by the authorities on individuals who violate the law, that is, as long as the authorities enforce the law on journalists, he considers that it is a restriction on the freedom of the press.
And secondly, this report fails to look at other aspects related to the profession of journalists, especially in relation to the exercise of the rights and freedoms of journalists, whether it is in accordance with the legal framework and the profession of journalists. The body or not? Such an assessment method is inaccurate, incomplete and unscientific.
Mr. Kim Santepheap: In the red area, people are not allowed to go to the market and there is no permit to go to the market
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Justice, on April 23 came out to reject the distortion that there was a distribution of cards that allow people to go to the food market in the red zone during the implementation of the closure measures. Block and restrict travel.
