Malai District Police Inspector confirmed that according to the explanation of the six workers, they were dropped by the driver of a silver taxi in front of Vihear Cham in Chrey Village, Boeung Beng Commune, then two brokers Crossing O Den to Thailand at Chrey village, Boeung Beng commune, crossing into Thai waters about 2 km, was captured by Thai soldiers and sent back.
As for the confessions of the two brokers, they replied that they had actually sent the six Cambodian workers across the border into Thailand for 200 baht each.
Colonel Lay Kim Loun, director of the Anti-Human Trafficking and Juvenile Protection Police Office, confirmed that the two suspects had been sent to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court for legal action. As for the six Cambodian workers, two females, the Malai district police sent them to the Talat Sak center in Malai district for 14 days before they could return home.
