The three people who were declared dead by the Ministry of Health in 19 are:
* First, the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital said that a 55-year-old Cambodian man living in Sangkat Phsar Thmei 2, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, was admitted to the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital on April 11, 2021. At 22:05 pm, after receiving a positive result, Kovid-19 with severe asthma condition, which required a medical team to provide emergency medical treatment.
As the patient's condition worsens from day to day until April 18, 2021, doctors need to use a ventilator, despite the efforts of doctors to provide technical assistance. Still unable to rescue the patient, he died on April 21, 2021 at 16:30 pm.
* Second: Calmette Hospital said that an 83-year-old Cambodian woman living in Sangkat Phsar Kandal 1, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh was admitted to Calmette Hospital on April 21, 2021 at 13:20 with Excessive shortness of breath and airway obstruction, which required a team of doctors to provide technical assistance and take samples for analysis, the results showed a positive Kovid-19.
As the patient's condition worsened, the patient died at 2:00 p.m.
* Third: Victory Referral Hospital said that an 81-year-old Cambodian woman living in Takhmao City, Kandal Province was admitted to Victory Referral Hospital on April 14, 2021 at 5:30 pm. Exhausted after getting a positive Kovid-19.
As the patient's condition worsened day by day, the medical team had to provide immediate technical assistance, including the use of a ventilator, but could not save the patient, and he died. On April 21, 2021 at 09:10 in the morning.
According to the doctors, the three Cambodian men and women died of acute respiratory distress and severe pneumonia caused by the Kovid-19 virus. The Ministry of Health would like to express its deepest condolences and condolences to the bereaved family.
