WASHINGTON (Reuters) - North Korea may be trying to develop a weapons capability that could reduce the effectiveness or override the US missile defense system deployed in Local. This was released by Yonhap News Agency on Thursday, April 22, 2021.
"The latest step in North Korea's ballistic missile test program seems to be aimed at developing capabilities to reduce "Or overcome the effectiveness of the US missile system deployed in the region, including the THAAD system."
The report notes that the KN-23 short-range ballistic missile that North Korea test-fired last month could hit any location on the Korean Peninsula, and that the test could be a test of a new KN-23 missile. It makes it difficult to intercept. The CRS report added that North Korea could also focus on developing submarine-launched ballistic missiles to overcome US missile defense systems in the region.
