MOSCOW, April 21 (Xinhua) - Russian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday issued a stern warning to Western countries against violating Russia's security interests, saying Moscow's response would be "swift". And very strong. This is according to the release by the AP news agency on Wednesday, April 21, 2021.
Putin's warning came during his annual address and comes amid a massive military build-up on Ukraine's border, where a ceasefire has been violated in a seven-year conflict. Between Russian-backed separatists and Ukrainian forces has escalated in recent weeks. The United States and its allies have urged the Kremlin to withdraw troops from the area.
"I hope no one dares to cross the red line regarding Russia," Putin said. And we will determine where it is in each specific case. "Anyone who tries to provoke something that threatens Russia's core security interests will feel remorse for their unprecedented actions."
Moscow has dismissed concerns from Ukraine and the West over troop deployments along the border between the two countries, saying it does not threaten anyone and that Russia is free to deploy its forces on its territory. Its.
The Kremlin has also warned Ukrainian authorities against using force to seize rebel-held eastern areas, saying Russia could be forced to intervene to protect civilians in the region.
