Special forces plan to retrieve unexploded ordnance that sank with a ship during the civil war at Boeung Krom, Lvea Em district next week
(Phnom Penh): Major General Mey Sophea, Commander of the Underwater Explosive Ordnance Disposal Clearance Command, confirmed to Fresh News that on April 21, 2021, the specialized force launched a search operation to A ship carrying unexploded ordnance that sank during the Civil War and is scheduled to be retrieved next week.
The second site was built in the presence of General Neang Phat, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense and Chair of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group to study and resolve the case of unexploded ordnance found in a ship that sank in the river. March 15, 2021 ago.
Lt. Gen. Mey Sophea stated: "In connection with the operation at Boeung Krom, we are continuing the search. Now we have found the location of the shipwreck and the point of unexploded ordnance early next week. Now we are preparing the means. "Equipment to suit the size of the operation as well as the actual situation in the operating area."
"So next week we will begin to search for the location of the shipwreck and unexploded ordnance, and hopefully next week we will be able to begin retrieving more and more ammunition," he added.
According to General Neang Phat, the operation to clear unexploded ordnance buried under the water at this point is an unprecedented historical achievement for Cambodia and also shows that Cambodia has the ability to not only clear The ammunition has not yet exploded on the mainland, so it is another source of pride for the Cambodian nation.
According to General Neang Phat, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's location allowed the team to continue researching for munitions that sank with warships during the civil war, including:
Location 1: Located in Roka Kong Muy village, Prek Dambang commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province, a type of boat transporting weapons and ammunition of Lon Nol soldiers, which sank during 1972.
Location 2: In Boeung Kaek village, Peam Meanchey commune, Peam Ro district, Prey Veng province, loaded with weapons and ammunition of Lon Nol army with a capacity of 1,000 tons.
And the third location: in Peam Reang village, Koh Chek commune, Peam Ro district, Prey Veng province, a warship with a capacity of about 1,000 tons was fired and exploded during the war from 1972 to 1973. Samdech Chao Feang Kong Sam Ol and Lok Chumteav Donate US $ 5,000 on the Occasion of the 158th Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2021
