10,000 Chinese in Cambodia have been vaccinated
(Phnom Penh): The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia has confirmed that about 10,000 people are living and working in Cambodia and have been vaccinated the first dose by April 20, 2021. According to the Chinese embassy, those who received the vaccine included China, Hong Kong, Macau and Taiwan.
The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, on behalf of the Chinese people in Cambodia, expressed its deep gratitude to the institutions in Cambodia, including the Ministry of Health, the Ministry of National Defense, Preah Keto Mealea Hospital, as well as to the efforts of the working group of the Secretariat of the Chamber of Commerce. Chinese production in Cambodia, which facilitated the vaccination process.
It should be noted that during the outbreak of Kovid 19 for more than a year, we have shown close cooperation and support in the fight against Kovid 19. The government provided medical equipment, testing equipment, 19 Kovid samples, provided 1.3 million doses of the Sinofam vaccine, and facilitated the purchase of 2 million doses of the Sinovak vaccine at a lower cost.
The Chinese government, through the embassy, has expressed its position that it will continue to support Cambodia until it succeeds in the fight against Kovid 19.
