(Preah Vihear): Police in Preah Vihear province on April 20, 2021 sent four youths to temporary prisons after they smuggled through Preah Vihear and Oddar Meanchey provinces in violation of the ban. Of the Royal Government to temporarily suspend travel from one province to another to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
The transfer of the four young men to a temporary prison was coordinated by Mr. Vuth Savy, Deputy Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
"The four young men were detained by the Preah Vihear Provincial Gendarmerie at the border between Preah Vihear and Oddar Meanchey provinces," he said. According to the confessions of these four people, they live in Sraem commune, Choam Ksan district, and stole across the border to Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province, riding a motorbike through the forest, and when they returned, they borrowed a friend's car and were arrested by the police.
According to the Deputy Prosecutor, Article 11 of the first paragraph of the law on measures to prevent the spread of the deadly and dangerous disease of Kovid-19, it is imperative that the law and measures be implemented. To prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
After detaining four youths and sending them to a temporary prison, the Deputy Prosecutor called on all parents to educate their children well not to violate the law as well as regulations issued to prevent infection. The spread of Kovid-19 in our country. CEC-19 Commission Selects the Office of the Ministry of Tourism as the Site for the Second Sinovac Vaccination for Citizens and Civil Servants Living in Khan 7 Makara
