(Svay Rieng): A factory building collapsed and 7 other villagers' houses opened their roofs due to heavy rain, thunder and strong winds at 3 pm on April 19, 2021 in 6 districts in Svay Rieng province Fortunately, no one was injured.
Sources from Svay Rieng provincial authorities said that the six districts in Svay Rieng province affected by rain mixed with strong winds include:
1: Chantrea district, located in Trapeang Bon village, Prey Korki commune, caused the collapse of a factory building made of steel with a size of 100 meters X87 meters, height 12 meters, causing complete damage, but did not cause any casualties.
2. In Romduol district, located at Trapeang Kandol village, Men Chey commune, the roof of the house of two families named Hing Un, female, 42 years old, house size 6m x 7m, made of wood, damaged some tiles. And the owner of the house, Yus Sitha, a 45-year-old man, measuring 6 x 7 meters, made of wood, with a galvanized roof and some materials.
3: Svay Teap district, at Kak village, Svay Rumpear commune, Svay Teap district, the roof of Ek Vuthy's house, female, 50 years old, farmer, was opened. The leaves will damage some rice husks.
4: Svay Chrum district, the owner of the house is Ung Vuthy Pros, 46 years old, a farmer living in Daun Tong village, Thlok commune, Svay Chrum district, causing a tree to fall on the house, causing complete damage to the house, zinc roof, 4m x 6m galvanized wall and the owner Second: Sam Eam, female, living in Svay Ang village, Svay Ang commune, Svay Chrum district, caused the roof of the house to be 6 meters x 4 meters wide.
5: Kampong Ror district, the owner is Noun Thon, male, 81 years old, residing in Samyong village, Samyong commune, causing some damage to the zinc opening without affecting life and other property.
6: Romeas Hek district, the owner of the house is Say Khara, male, 35 years old, and his wife is Khim Srey Chen, 24 years old, living in Prey Srah village, Sambath Meanchey commune, the house size is 6m X7m This does not affect or endanger people.
