China does not understand that a strong country will have to do supremacy, but firmly believes that a supremacy country will shrink.
BEIJING, April 16 (Xinhua) - Chinese Vice Foreign Minister Le Yucheng said in an exclusive interview with the Associated Press on April 16 that the two countries will continue to work together for the development of China-US relations. And China's foreign policy that peaceful development is the cornerstone of China's diplomacy and enshrined in China's constitution.
With China's rapid development, China's international role and influence continue to grow. But despite development and change, China's policy of independent and peaceful diplomacy will not change, and the policy of non-hegemony, non-expansion and non-interference in the internal affairs of other countries will not change. Also.
We are more glorious and prosperous than before, but we are not arrogant or overbearing. We do not see that a strong country will prevail, but we strongly believe that a superpower will decrease.
China's development is not to win or replace anyone, nor to compete with others to become the world's greatest, but to improve the lives of the Chinese people and Promote the building of a common community of human destiny.
Cambodia, Canada discuss 4 points on law and justice for future cooperation
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chin Malin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Justice, led a working group of the Ministry of Justice of Cambodia to meet with representatives of the Canadian Embassy in Cambodia and the Ministry of Justice in Canada to discuss four points on law and justice. Looking forward to future cooperation.
Discuss four points on law and justice, including:
* First, the development of a policy and legal framework related to legal aid and out-of-court dispute resolution in Cambodia. * Second: Strengthening the capacity of Ministry of Justice officials and officials in the tribunal * Third: Strengthening training and research institutions in the field of law and justice and Fourth: Modernizing the administration of the judiciary.
Jin Malin confirmed that the working group will continue to work together to discuss and exchange documents with each other in order to achieve cooperation in the near future.
