Phnom Penh Court of Appeal Receives Telegraphic Appeal During Implementation of Travel Bans and Prohibitions
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Court of Appeal on April 20, 2021, issued a press release on the receipt of appeals by electronic means (telegram) in advance during the implementation of measures to block and ban travel in Cambodia. This is according to a press release obtained by Fresh News.
In order to avoid losing the right to appeal by the parties to the case at the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal due to the inability to travel to file a complaint in person, the parties can file a appeal by electronic means (telegram) at any business hours from 8:30 am By 16:30 pm and there will be people in charge of the following types of stories:
To file an appeal through the above telegram, the parties must meet the following conditions:
* 1: This complaint must specify the identity of the plaintiff or the lawyer represented by the legal mandate.
* 2: Specify the case number, judgment number, order, date, case type, side of the case, type of appeal, reason of appeal, date of dismissal.
* 3: The other party must record the complaint, ID card, phone number sent to the above telegram.
* 4: The appellant can send the documents through this telegram to the appellate party, such as the order to pay the case file, the submission of the reason for the appellation, etc., so the appellate party must make this work in advance to implement.
* 5: The appealing party must apply in writing and fulfill the conditions of the appeal at the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal as soon as possible and meet the conditions in point 4 above after the closure of the Royal Government is completed and to ensure that The Court of Appeal will deal with you as soon as possible.
