UPDATE: A military officer who was arrested when he hit a police barracks has a mental problem because he had a car accident that killed a family member and his children, his wife became mentally ill and divorced
(Phnom Penh): A military officer who was arrested when he hit a police barracks had a mental problem because he had a car accident that killed a family member and his children, and after this horrific incident, his wife became mentally ill and divorced.
According to a letter from Calmette Hospital and Preah Kosomak Hospital, obtained by Fresh News, Khieu Chan Sopheaktra is indeed mentally ill and requires daily medication.
The reason why this person has brain and mental illness is because during 2016, he was involved in a car accident on National Road 48 in Koh Kong province, resulting in the death of his family, two brothers-in-law and his unborn child. He later divorced his wife and she had the same memory problem.
Regarding this case, General Dr. Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner, told Fresh News this morning, April 20, 2021, he has not yet made a decision, leaving the judiciary to make a legal decision after Authorities refer to the court.
It should be informed that the police force of Chroy Changvar district on the morning of April 20, 2021, handcuffed this military officer after driving a motorbike and hitting a barricade and using violence against the target police. The suspect, a military officer, will be arraigned in court.
San Sok Seiha, an assistant and spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, told Fresh News that the perpetrator was Khieu Chan Sopheaktra, 31, a military official at the Ministry of National Defense. He confirmed that the perpetrator hit the barricade, closed, blocked, insulted and insulted the police. Authorities are now bringing the district inspector for questioning and preparing a file to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
