(Kampot): Two Chinese nationals faked driving an ambulance with the intention of passing through Kampot to Sihanoukville, violating the Royal Government's instruction to block the passage of passengers from one province to another, which was arrested by the police. He was sent to Kampot Provincial Court for sentencing before being deported from Cambodia.
On April 19, 2021, the Kampot Provincial Court issued a detention order for both of them.
Speaking to Fresh News on April 20, 2021, Kampot Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Mao Chanthurith said that after the end of the interrogation of the two Chinese nationals, the case was built to Sent to court for conviction and then deported from Cambodia later.
It should be informed that this operation, the Kampot Immigration Police Force led by Brigadier General Sem Sophoan cooperated with the professional police to detain the two Chinese nationals since April 14, 2021.
However, at the time of arrest, only preliminary interrogation was required, as the sample had to be examined first to proceed with further procedures. When the result was negative, the specialized police force proceeded with the procedure. Currently, on April 17, 2021, the immigration planning force sent the two Chinese nationals to the deportation office in Sihanoukville for deportation. Leave Cambodia immediately.
Lt. Gen. Mao Thurith confirmed that on the day of the incident, the two Chinese nationals tried to drive an ambulance with the logo "Chong Sin Hospital" across the border between Kampot and Sihanoukville provinces when the police interrogated them. The car ran back and was then detained by special forces at the intersection of Bokor Mountain in Kep Thmey Village, Boeung Touk Commune, Teuk Chhou District, Kampot Province.
