Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted this in his opening remarks at the Boa Forum for Asia, which was held via video. The forum is entitled "The World in Change: Working Together to Strengthen Global Governance and Promote Belt and Road Cooperation."
In the presence of the leaders of the member countries of the Boao Forum for Asia, a forum initiated by China, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia said that in the context of the Kovid 19 crisis and the geopolitical challenges of this great country, each country Should play a more active role in global governance with flexibility, constructiveness and a responsible attitude.
"Under these circumstances, I understand that the world really needs a global governance that supports multilateralism and respects international law and the sovereignty of individual countries, regardless of size or resources, with the United Nations," he said. At the core. "Cambodia recognizes the central role of multilateralism in addressing complex and interconnected global challenges."
In his opening remarks, Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the Chinese government's Belt and Road Initiative. Samdech Techo underlined that under the Belt and Road Initiative since its inception, it has contributed to the promotion of regional and global cooperation on hard and soft infrastructure, economy, trade, investment opportunities, cultural exchanges and trade. Connect between people and people.
He said that in the face of this economic downturn, the Belt and Road Initiative remains a driving force to further expand cooperation among countries in the region and the world for the cause of peace, security, prosperity and sustainable development. .
On behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his deep gratitude to the Government and people of China for providing 3.3 million doses of medicine, medical equipment as well as Kovid-19 vaccine to Cambodia. Of that, 1.3 million doses is humanitarian aid.
Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Opening Ceremony of the Boao Forum for Asia via Video (2 pages) (Phnom Penh): The Boao Forum for Asia 20th Anniversary was officially opened on the morning of April 20, 2021 in China. . The opening ceremony was attended by leaders of member countries, including Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Due to the crisis of Kovid 19, the opening of this forum could not be as grand as in previous years, only through the video system.
Boao Forum for Asia (BFA) is an international non-profit organization based in China and is the most famous and important Boao Forum for Asia for leaders from government, business and universities in Asia and beyond. Share perspectives on key issues in potential regions around the world.
In 2021, the forum will be held under the theme "The World in Change: Working Together to Strengthen Global Governance and Promote Belt and Road Cooperation."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen congratulated the 20th anniversary of the establishment of this forum. Samdech Techo emphasized that for the past 20 years, this forum has made significant contributions to promoting political, economic, social, cultural and environmental cooperation.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia also stated that currently Kovi-19 continues to pose a serious threat to global public health and overall development. In this context, no country is safe unless all countries are safe.
In this speech, Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised China's high attention and commitment to implement the "Health Silk Road" under the Belt and Road Initiative and its leading role in providing medicine. Timely delivery of Kovid-19 medical equipment and vaccines to many countries, which is a clear testament to China's global leadership.
On behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, Samdech Techo expressed his deep gratitude to the Government and people of China for providing 3.3 million doses of medicine, medical equipment as well as Kovid-19 vaccine to Cambodia. That 1.3 million doses is humanitarian aid.
