(Phnom Penh): On April 20, 2021, tomorrow, the Ministry of Commerce is ready to release food trucks to sell in the closed areas (red area) in 7 places in Khan Meanchey, Khan Por Sen Chey and Khan Toul Kork for sale. To the people at a lower price than the market in accordance with the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Speaking to Fresh News on the night of April 19, 2021, Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Commerce, confirmed that according to the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Minister of Commerce further recommended the company Green Trade urges to act quickly and in a timely manner to address the plight of the people who are implementing blockade measures in the red areas in the three districts of Phnom Penh.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat stated, "This morning, all five mobile vehicles of the Ministry of Commerce, along with some other mobile vehicles of Phnom Penh Capital Hall, will go out to sell at all 7 locations in the red area in Khan Meanchey, Khan Por Sen Chey and Khan Toul Kork.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce pointed out that the goods that will be on sale tomorrow at lower prices than the market price include: rice, noodles, pure water, canned fish, fish sauce, soy sauce. And the Ministry of Commerce is preparing to add more essential goods to meet the needs of the people in this difficult time, such as dried fish, fried fish, beets and other strategic foods that can be stored for a long time.
At the same time, he said that the Ministry will continue to monitor the stability of sources of supply and prevent the increase in prices, which is carried out regularly in markets and other outlets, which is carried out by the team to monitor sources of supply to prevent rising prices. , Officer of General Department of Commerce and Department of Commerce, Phnom Penh and Kandal Province.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat stated that this work was also carried out to respond immediately to the questions and requests of the people provided through the telegram of the working group in response to questions related to the closure measures with representatives of the Ministry. Member Trade.
Please be informed that through an urgent instruction on detailed measures to restrict the implementation during the closure (LOCKDOWN) of Phnom Penh and Takhmao City on April 19, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia The Ministry of Commerce must immediately coordinate the supply, transportation and distribution of food and other essential foodstuffs for sale to people living in the "Red Zone".
The instruction of the Head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, stated that "The Ministry of Commerce must immediately coordinate the supply, transportation and distribution of food, including rice, noodles, canned fish, fish sauce, soy sauce and pure water and accessories. "Other essential groceries to sell to people living in the red zone by using telephone or online sales and home delivery."
On April 15, 2021, the Ministry of Commerce started selling rice and noodles in Phnom Penh at a lower price than the market to facilitate people by limiting the purchase of a bag of rice and a case of noodles per family.
For 5 days from April 15-19, 2021, the Ministry of Commerce's mobile vehicles sold a total of 297 sacks of rice, 1975 boxes of noodles, 136 sticks of fish sauce and soy sauce to people in the closed area of the capital. Phnom Penh and Takhmao at lower prices than the market.
