BEIJING: The United States and Japan have no right or inadequacy to represent the international community to set international order or set their own standards for others, a Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman said Monday. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Monday, April 19, 2021.
Spokesman Wang Wenbin made the remarks at a news conference when asked to comment on China-related issues in a joint statement issued by the United States and Japan on Tuesday. Recently.
Raising human rights issues, Wang said Japan and the United States owed the people of China and the world, emphasizing the catastrophe that affected the people of China and Asia due to Japan's war of aggression in the 1930s and war. The United States has been relegated to foreign lands, killing more than 800,000 people since 2001, including 300,000 civilians.
Meanwhile, the Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman added that US policy on COVID-19 has not only hurt the American people, but also created obstacles for international cooperation. In the fight against the universe.
