(Phnom Penh): The announcement of the Ministry of Health on April 19, 2021 states that those who need to be vaccinated with Kovid 19 second dose must show the first vaccination card and Cambodian identity card or passport or birth certificate. Or family book, residence book or Chhaya to the officer at the vaccination site in the district where he / she is living.
In the event that the documents are not seized due to government blockade measures, the individual may present these documents electronically. This means that the person only has to take the necessary documents, especially the first immunization card and ID card via mobile phone to show to the officer as a decision.
The Ministry of Health added that the competent authority of the vaccination site should issue a certificate stating that the person was vaccinated against the second dose of Kovid 19, in which the name, date of birth, sex, address of the person and the date and place of vaccination must be written. The second dose of vaccine and the name of the second dose of vaccine given at its location, as well as the name of the person responsible for issuing the certificate and signed.
Due to the Royal Government's measures to block people from passing through the provinces and the capital, the Ministry of Health has issued a new notification on the process of vaccinating the second dose at the local residents without having to go. Get vaccinated where they were first vaccinated.
