Cambodian Aquaculture Association Explains Rising Retail Fish Prices in the Market and Asks Authorities to Facilitate Fish Transportation
Meanwhile, some media and social media users have incorrectly concluded that the increase was due to Cambodia's lack of fish to supply the market and demanded the opening of large-scale fish imports from neighboring countries. Also.
The Cambodian Fishermen's Association would like to inform you that at present, our fishermen all over the country have thousands of tons of clogged fish in the pond since January 2021, as stated in the press release on April 1, 2021. Here, the sale price from the pond of our hydropower brothers is not increased at all.
Retail fish prices in the market have recently risen due to:
1. The transportation of fishery products by road to the distribution depot in Phnom Penh is facing many difficulties due to the closure of traffic, which causes delays.
2. Small distributors in the provinces around Phnom Penh and in Phnom Penh find it difficult to travel to the fishery product distribution center in Phnom Penh to receive all kinds of fish to distribute in the markets.
3. Illegal fish imports and fraud can not be done as much as before.
The Cambodian Fishermen's Association urges law enforcement agencies and relevant institutions to continue to restrict the import of illegal fish and to facilitate the transportation, fishing in ponds and the reception of fish for distribution to markets. Ensure the supply of fish in the markets returns to normal.
The Cambodian Fishermen's Association will cooperate with all traders at any time if they want to get the contact number of the fish farmers, the place where the fish are sold and the type of fish in the pond that can be caught for sale. Do not want to try drugs even half a time! Nationwide drug crackdown for April 19: 14 cases cracked, 25 arrested
