Conversation with ancient generations through crafts
Guangzhou: The ancient site of Shantou, located in Guangzhou, Sichuan Province, China, has a history of 3,000 to 5,000 years, and is the largest and oldest cultural archeological site. The deepest in southwestern China is considered to be one of the greatest archaeological discoveries of mankind in the 20th century.
On March 20, 2021, the achievements of a new round of archeological excavations were announced. Of the more than 500 important artifacts, only half of the gold mass remains intriguing, with netizens experimenting with assembling the entire gold mass through Photoshop. The cut paper shows the whole face of the golden mass through the cut paper image and is highly appreciated by the internet users.
On April 12, a 25-year-old appletter named Chhay Chhean uploaded a video clip to the Bilibili website to share his handmade gold mask journey. When the news about the half-gold mass was spread, netizens gathered the other half-mass, and Chhay Chhean was very interested and wanted to try it out for himself.
In the process of making a hammer weighing 1.8 kg, the fastest and most powerful hammer was hit more than 10,000 times. The production of the golden mass was almost completed by Chhay Chhean alone, with another person helping. Meanwhile, there was one who filmed the entire production process to share with netizens the fascination of the craft.
Chhay Chhean is good at carving knives and swords in all kinds of wooden cartoons. He is known as the master of the iron world. No matter how strange the sword and the knife, he can do it cleverly. So where did he learn such a craft? In fact, his next major in university was e-news, handicraft, and he learned relevant knowledge online.
