Police in Ratanakkiri Province seize an ambulance belonging to a private clinic that was smuggling people from Phnom Penh
(Ratanakkiri): Police in Ratanakkiri Province seized an ambulance belonging to a private clinic that was illegally transporting people from Phnom Penh in violation of the Royal Government's instruction to ban transit from one province to another. At the time of the outbreak, Kovid 19 was infected.
According to the report from Ratanakkiri province, on the morning of April 19, 2021, on the night of April 17, 2021, after receiving information from the Banlung municipal authorities, the joint police force stationed to prevent Kovid-19 disease at the bridge Sre Pok, on the border of Stung Treng province, in cooperation with the local authority of Kon Mom district, stopped the case of crossing the province (Phnom Penh-Ratanakkiri) by taking refuge under an ambulance.
According to a report from the police, the ambulance was privately owned by a doctor, a monk and a paramedic who transported two people, Kheang Channy and But Bun Reaksa, for $ 600 from his doctor. The monks came to Ratanakkiri province and the Banlung municipal authorities stopped them from returning to Kon Mom district authorities for further action.
Currently, the driver and the van have been detained by the Kon Mom District Military Police in order to carry out the operation and proceed according to the procedures. Separately, the two passengers were sent to the center of Trapeang Krahorm, Kon Mom district to do the procession.
