In the instruction of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, which Fresh News received that to participate in the effective implementation of Resolution No. 50 Pillar dated 17 April 2021 on the adjustment of measures to be taken during the closure. Block the geography of Phnom Penh and Takhmao City of Kandal Province to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and to ensure the sustainability of the necessary work, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport will issue four guidelines, including:
* First, all units under the Ministry must reduce the number of civil servants who are on duty and complete the necessary work to only 2% (2%) and must apply the principle of lunch at the place of work. For other civil servants who are not assigned to be on duty must work from home through the online system (Online) as assigned by the head of each unit.
* Second: The leaders of the Ministry and the staff of the civil servants who must come to perform the necessary work as assigned must have a mission order for traveling through the geographical area of Phnom Penh. The mission order must be signed by the Senior Minister, the Minister of Public Works and Transport or Mr. Suy San, Secretary of State.
The procedures and procedures for issuing mission orders to ministry leaders and subordinates (2%) shall be as follows:
- For HE-Lok Chumteav as the Leader of the Ministry, to be signed by HE Senior Minister, Minister of Public Works and Transport directly-For HE General Department / Inspectorate and Permanent Civil Servants (2%) to be signed by HE Suy San, Secretary of State in charge Administrative affairs.
