Commentary: The US arbitrary interference in Hong Kong affairs is a violent violation of the rule of law.
BEIJING, April 16 (Xinhua) - A Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (SAR) official issued a statement on April 16 discussing the fair trial of a Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (SAR) judge on a number of crimes against China. The unrest in Hong Kong and the unreasonable demand for the Chinese side to release these criminals.
Those who took care of Hong Kong will never forget that on August 18, 2019, some extremist protesters in Hong Kong took up arms, set fire to the streets, attacked the police and insulted the flag. Is a violent demonstration a "peaceful demonstration"? The extremist protesters also surrounded and attacked ordinary people. Who is violating the freedom of Hong Kong people?
Thus, the Hong Kong court has given a fair trial and fair trial of the perpetrators against China and caused unrest in Hong Kong, fully demonstrating the spirit of the rule of law in Hong Kong and also in response to the demands of the Hong Kong people. Too crowded.
The United States, which claims to be a country of the "rule of law", has violated the principle of non-interference in the internal affairs of other countries and has angrily interfered in the fair trial of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, demanding the release of criminals. These things are a trampling on the spirit of the rule of law as a whole.
The situation in Hong Kong has stabilized, and some of the trial of anti-China criminals and riots in Hong Kong will go on the agenda. The fierce US intervention and distortion will make it clear to the world that they are interfering in Hong Kong affairs, wanting to destabilize Hong Kong and cause chaos in China, but it is clear that the United States has stepped in. The dead end is a war of words.
