The announcement of the presidential election was made by the Speaker of the Syrian National Assembly, Hamouda Sabbagh. According to Hamuda, the election to elect a president to lead the country for a seven-year term will be held on May 26. He added that all presidential candidates will be able to register to run in the by-elections from Monday, and that Syrians abroad could vote in the Syrian parliament on May 20.
This is the second presidential election to be held during the Syrian civil war. The 2014 election, in which Assad received 92 percent of the vote, was considered undemocratic by the United States and the European Union, and in this year's election, Assad is expected to remain in power. At the same time, his government is in control of almost all of the territory.
