Director of Svay Rieng Provincial Health Department urges Kovid doctors to pay attention to professional ethics in treating patients effectively
(Svay Rieng): Dr. Ker Ratha, Director of Svay Rieng Provincial Health Department, urges Kovid-19 physicians in the province to pay attention to and respect professional ethics in treating patients effectively and transparently. Make sure you get well soon.
Dr. Ker Ratha's encouragement was made on the occasion that he led a team of 17 doctors from Svay Taep Referral Hospital to take turns in the group of doctors in Kovid-19 Medical Center, Bavet City, who had to complete 14 tasks. Days.
The shift of Kovid-19 medical team took place on the afternoon of April 18, 2021, with the participation of Deputy Governor of Bavet City, Dr. Prak Sambath, Director of Chi Phu Referral Hospital, Dr. Sor Sok Chamroeun, President Svay Teap Referral Hospital and Dr. Im Bot, Head of Chattalysak Division.
On that occasion, Dr. Ker Ratha thanked all the Kovid-19 doctors in Svay Rieng province who worked hard to treat Kovid-19 patients without fear of exhaustion for the cause of the nation in this time. This is especially difficult to improve the well-being of the people.
Dr. Ker Ratha said that currently in Svay Rieng province, there are 2 Kovid-19 treatment hospitals and 1 Kovid-19 treatment center in Bavet city. At the two Kovid-19 treatment hospitals, the provincial governor and chairman of the Kovid-19 Provincial Commission used Svay Chrum Referral Hospital and Samaki Romduol Referral Hospital in Rumduol district to treat Kovid-19 patients.
He said that due to the increase in Kovid-19 patients, the provincial governor converted a building in Bavet City into a Kovid-19 treatment center. For the medical team in this clinic, the health department has moved from other hospitals in the province to help by changing shifts every 14 days.
Apparently, today, the doctors of Svay Taep Referral Hospital joined the doctors of Chi Phu Referral Hospital. However, the doctors of Chi Phu Referral Hospital had to stay in Chattalysak for another 14 days before being allowed to go home to meet their families. For the next turn, the team of doctors from Romeas Referral Hospital to the doctors of Svay Rieng Provincial Referral Hospital.
At the same time, Dr. also donated 20 lots of raw milk and 20 cases of pure water to the two groups of doctors and supported 4 people, each of whom received 50,000 Riels.
