Commentary: China's economy recovers steadily with strong resilience
BEIJING, April 16 (Xinhua) - China's gross domestic product (GDP) reached 24.931 trillion yuan in the first quarter of this year, according to official data released on Tuesday. 18.3 percent compared to the same period of 2020. Undoubtedly, the Chinese economy is a good start this year.
After undergoing the same period last year, China's economy has recovered steadily and has shown strong resilience, leading the way in the world's major economic entities. . This is because China has had a relatively successful recovery and has recovered on a low basis.
Of course, given the outbreak of Kovid 19 and the complicated international environment, China's economic recovery remains under pressure, but if analyzed, many factors in China's current economic development can It is believed that the world's largest economy is expected to maintain a steady recovery, while the global economic recovery will also be given more momentum by China.
