On the other hand, the 14 days of closure is also an important measure to measure Cambodia's success or failure in the fight against Kovid-19. And success or failure depends entirely on the participation of all citizens, that is, if all Cambodians are patient and participate in implementing this measure consistently, the event of February 20 may end soon.
On the other hand, if the people lack patience and do not participate in the implementation, the great catastrophe will come, then we will all suffer in the long run, which is difficult to recover and difficult to find a definite end. Of course. Therefore, in order to overcome this deadly disease, the most effective measure is to consistently implement the three preventive measures that the Royal Government has already put in place.
