10 Sangkats in Takhmao City Receive Donations from Dr. Tep Ngorn, Second Vice President of the Senate
(Phnom Penh): In order to help alleviate the hardships of the people during the time of Cambodia experiencing Kovid 19, especially when the Royal Government decided to block Phnom Penh and Takhmao to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, Mr. Kitti Dr. Tep Ngorn, Second Vice President of the Senate, on the afternoon of April 17, 2021, led a delegation to distribute rice donations to 10 districts in Takhmao City, Kandal Province, which were closed.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Kitti Sangkhab Dr. Tep Ngorn addressed the greetings from Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate to the authorities at all levels, Sangkat Councilors and people throughout Takhmao City.
Dr. also wished the authorities at all levels, Sangkat councilors and people throughout Takhmao City to be safe during the traditional New Year and to be healthy and avoid all diseases, especially Kovid 19. .
Czech Republic gives 48 hours for 18 Russian diplomats to leave the country
The Czech Republic has expelled 18 Russian diplomats, accusing Moscow of involvement in an arsenal explosion in 2014. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Sunday, April 18, 2021.
In a statement released this weekend (local time), Czech Interior Minister and Acting Foreign Minister Jan Hamacek confirmed that the expulsion of the Russian diplomat followed. The Czech authorities identified them as members of the Russian intelligence service and they had 48 hours to leave the Czech Republic.
According to Czech media, the decision to fire the Russian diplomat was in response to evidence obtained by the Czech intelligence service that Russia was involved in an arsenal explosion in the Czech Republic in 2014. The lives of two people. US, China vow to work together to resolve climate crisis
China and the United States have agreed to work together to combat climate change ahead of a new round of international meetings scheduled for the end of 2021. This is according to a joint statement quoted by Reuters on Sunday, April 18, 2021.
The Paris Climate Agreement has urged all countries in the world to be as committed as possible to tackling climate change, and China has already pledged to do more to achieve this. The goal is to become a "carbon neutral country by 2060".
