France to host travelers from four countries
PARIS (Reuters) - France will crack down on travelers from Argentina, Brazil, Chile and South Africa over fears of a new mutant COVID-19 virus as it struggles with a new wave of the deadly disease. This is according to the Office of the Prime Minister of France, quoted by the AFP news agency on Sunday, April 18, 2021.
The French Prime Minister's Office said that although flights from Argentina, Chile and South Africa would not be suspended, all passengers from these countries would have to undergo a 10-day probationary period. Flights from Brazil have been suspended until next Friday due to concerns over the new P1 mutation virus, which can spread rapidly and potentially infect people who have been infected with its original COVID-19 virus. .
