Ministry of Health announces the case of two Cambodians who died of Kovid 19, a 70-year-old and a 48-year-old woman
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health announced the case of two Cambodians who died of Kovid 19, a 70-year-old man and a 48-year-old woman, according to a statement issued on April 17, 2021.
The Ministry of Health would like to inform the public that according to the report from:
1: Luang Mey Hospital said that a 48-year-old Cambodian woman living in Kampong Thom province was sampled on April 16, 2021 with a positive result of Kovid-19 with severe shortness of breath. The patient was taken to Luang Mey Hospital at 22:20 on the same day. Upon arrival at the hospital, the medical team found that the patient had already died before entering the hospital.
Doctors' conclusion: A 48-year-old Cambodian woman died of Kovid-19 before being admitted to hospital.
Doctors' conclusion: A 70-year-old Cambodian man died at home due to Kovid-19 in a diabetic.
The Ministry of Health would like to express its deepest condolences and condolences to the bereaved family. On the first day of implementing the measures to block communes in Siem Reap, there were some misunderstandings and divisions.
(Siem Reap): On April 17, 2021, the Siem Reap Provincial Administration began to implement measures to block three communes in Siem Reap, including Svay Dangkum, Sala Kamroeuk and Siem Reap.
With the implementation of the first day measures, police forces, along with security guards, were deployed at the main entrances and exits in the three communes, with barricades crossing the main roads.
According to a survey by Fresh News reporters who went to the barricades, the implementation of the closure measures on the first day has caused some resentments and misunderstandings between the police and the people because some people have not been able to do so. Be aware of the measures taken by the provincial administration. At the same time, some target areas that put people on the stand also strictly enforce the decisions of the provincial administration.
However, the number of misunderstandings is small. The Siem Reap Provincial Administration has confirmed that all these issues will be resolved and will continue to seek the understanding and tolerance of the people for the implementation of this blockade, and join together to eliminate the spread of Kovid 19.
Please note that the Siem Reap Provincial Administration has decided to close the above three communes for 14 days, starting from April 17. To implement this measure, the provincial administration has set 35 gate targets implemented by the Joint Forces of the Municipal Administrative Unity Command in cooperation with the three Sangkat Administrative Unity Commands.
The closure was carried out to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 further after doctors tested the traders and residents directly and indirectly involved in Phsar Krom and Phsar Atvar and found positive results. Kovid 19 07 people.
However, during the closure, the provincial administration took into account the impact on the people and arranged for food to be distributed to the affected people. On April 17, the provincial administration also issued measures to prevent the rise in prices of consumer goods, foodstuffs and medicines to implement measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in Siem Reap province.
On the occasion of the administration's decision to close these three communes in the Old Market and Samaki Market, Siem Reap, the market owner also set up a security line to secure his market to closely monitor customers entering his market. Primary health check-up with temperature measurement and alcohol spray cleaning, which is the spirit of the market owner's participation in the fight against Kovid 19 disease.
(Phnom Penh): Kovid 19 disease of the February 20 community event continues to spread day by day, with only a few days left for two months.
A total of more than 5,000 people were diagnosed with the disease and 39 died. The Royal Government and the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority have made efforts to combat the most acute events, but the situation has not improved.
Finally, on April 14, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, decided to impose measures to block Phnom Penh and Takhmao for two weeks from zero on April 15 to 28.
The measure prohibits residents from leaving their homes day and night unless absolutely necessary. After the implementation of this measure, Phnom Penh, which used to be crowded with all kinds of vehicles due to the travel of people to do business, work and serve their other needs, has become very peaceful.
Such a state of calm would not have been possible if the people of this capital had not joined forces to fight Kovid 19. The Prime Minister has already announced that if the situation of the Kovid 19 epidemic does not improve, he will continue to delay the blockade.
Therefore, in order for the capital to become a noisy place with the noise of the people, by re-installing it, all the people in Phnom Penh must take part in implementing the measures and guidelines of the Royal Government and the authorities. In addition, we need to strengthen the spirit of the fight against Kovid 19 for everyone to fight so that the disease does not spread to ourselves, our families and in our community.
Khsach Kandal District Administration and the Navy Quick Reaction Team clarify and reject the advertisement that a woman born in Kovid escaped from Chattalysak Center to take care of her husband, who is a Marine at Lok Sang Hospital
(Phnom Penh): Khsach Kandal District Administration, Kandal Province and the Navy Quick Reaction Team of the Navy on April 17, 2021 issued a statement and completely rejected the posting on Facebook and sharing via Messenger that there are women A man named Kovid escaped from Chattalysak Center in Khsach Kandal District to see his husband, a naval officer at Preah Kosomak Hospital, called a monk, until he became infected with a group of doctors and patients there.
A Khsach Kandal district administration and a navy spokesman have categorically denied the allegations, saying that a Facebook post reported that a woman had fled the Khsach Kandal district center with 19 Kovid patients to visit her husband. He, who was in a car accident in Sihanoukville, is receiving emergency treatment at Preah Kosamak Hospital in Phnom Penh. This is not true information.
The district administration and the navy spokesperson would like to completely reject the case of spreading false information on Facebook via text message (Messenger) that there is a case of a woman named Em Sareth is the wife of the military. One who encountered the O'Brien explosion while on a mission in Sihanoukville.
In fact, Ms. Sareth, who currently has a positive Kovid 19 above, did not escape from the Chattalysak Center in Khsach Kandal District, Kandal Province, as advertised on social media, because according to the investigation to the location and The assertion of Mr. Bun Pheng, the governor of Khsach Kandal district and the district working group and Mr. Lim Phalla, the director of the district health office, is that there is no such name in Chattalysak district.
It should be noted that a woman named Met Sareth was in the house to take care of her children without going out and was not in any of the Chattalysak areas, but because her husband had an accident, she came to take care of her husband. Unfortunately, because his nephew, who came to visit him on April 5, 2021, went to test positive for Kovid 19, he went to test and found that he was also positive.
