General Vong Pisen issues orders to implement the blockade of Phnom Penh and Takhmao for the army
(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen has issued an order to implement the blockade of Phnom Penh and Takhmao City, Kandal Province to prevent the spread of 19 Kovid disease in the army. This is according to the letter from General Vong Pisen, which was received by Fresh News on the morning of April 17, 2021.
In the letter, General Vong Pisen issued the following five strict regulations:
* First, the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, the Director of Institutions and Sub-Committees of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces shall strictly implement Decision No. 49 / Pillar of the Head of the Royal Government and Circular No. 006 / SAN / 2021 of the Ministry of National Defense. On the closure of Phnom Penh and Takhmao, Kandal province to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
* Second, the institutions at the General Command are only staffed by officers who have to take turns commanding and stationing at a minimum to ensure the daily work of soldiers living in the Red Zone (the area with the highest number of Kovid infections) ) Must follow the rules of local authorities to the unit, do not allow soldiers to leave the unit.
* Third: The unit that has the duty to cooperate in closing this block must perform its role as strictly as possible and protect itself from the infection of Kovid 19.
* Fourth: Application period from the date of signing this agreement onwards.
* Fifth: The Director of the Cabinet of the General Command, the Commander of the Special Forces, the Director of Institutions and the School under the General Command of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces must implement this regulation effectively.
