Provincial Administration Warns to Shut Down Businesses or Withdraw Licenses of Any Place That Has Increased Prices During Closure of Some Areas in Siem Reap City
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Administration has warned to close all businesses or revoke the licenses of any locations that take the opportunity to increase prices during the closure of certain areas in Siem Reap City.
The warning was issued in accordance with the guidelines on measures to prevent the increase in prices of all kinds of food and medicine during the implementation of prevention of the spread of Kovid 19 on April 17, 2021.
Siem Reap Provincial Administration has instructed the owners or managers of companies, enterprises, distribution depots, restaurants, public places, private markets, supermarkets, supermarkets, pharmacies, beverages, food stalls, cafes, businesses, service centers and all kinds of shops, traders and citizens to follow the following instructions. Under:
First, do not increase the price of consumer goods, all kinds of food and medicine, the price is too high or too expensive, which affects the lives and livelihoods of the people.
Second, to implement hygiene measures, quality, food safety and consumer protection to participate in preventing the spread of Kovid 19 in the community
Third, prepare a mass of water, alcohol, soap or gel for hand washing and prepare a thermometer for customers and staff at the entrance every day, etc.
The provincial administration instructs the relevant units to monitor and business owners, and in case of excessive or excessive price increase, to take action to suspend or suspend or revoke the license temporarily or permanently and take legal action in force.
It should be noted that the Siem Reap Provincial Administration has decided to close three communes, including Sala Kamroeuk, Svay Dangkum and Siem Reap for two weeks from zero on April 16 to prevent the spread of 19 Kovid disease in the province and to To facilitate the livelihood of the people during this period, the Siem Reap Provincial Administration has advised not to increase the price of goods.
Comment: China's foreign trade continues to grow sharply
BEIJING, April 13 (Xinhua) - The Chinese government on Tuesday released data on China's foreign trade in the first quarter, showing a 29 percent increase in total exports and imports of goods. .2 percent compared to the same period last year, in which exports increased by 38.7 percent and imports increased by 19.3 percent.
China's foreign trade performance in the first quarter has maintained a positive growth trend since the fourth quarter of 2020, which achieved a "good starting point" in 2021.
The reasons for maintaining China's steady growth in foreign trade are not difficult to understand.
Exports can be seen that as the 199 Kovid vaccination framework has gradually expanded, the global economic recovery has shown positive trends. The World Trade Organization (WTO) recently raised its forecast for global trade in growth from 7.2 percent to 8 percent. Improved external demand has strongly boosted China's exports.
Imports show that China's manufacturing, investment and industrial consumption continue to recover, boosting imports. According to data released by the Chinese government, the recovery in manufacturing has further boosted imports of products such as integrated circuits and energy resources.
More importantly, China has effectively organized and managed the 19 prevention and control of Kovid disease and economic development to provide strong support for the steady and continuous process of foreign trade. At the same time, from the trade score of foreign trade, the external environment has also seen the positive trend brought about by China's push for higher-level openness.
Currently, the global economic situation is still complicated and tense, and the development of trade with foreign countries also faces many uncertainties and instability. But China will continue to push for reform and opening-up as planned, create more favorable conditions and keep foreign trade on a positive path to boost the global economy. Slowly. #CCFR Comment #
