In an audio message issued on April 16, 2021, Samdech Techo emphasized that there are still violators of the law and measures taken by the authorities in the fight against Kovid 19. Such as gatherings, drinking or stealing across the province.
For Samdech Techo, these people can not be excused. The Prime Minister stated, "I am pleased with the news that someone has violated the law and has been arrested and sent to court. "I urge the implementation of the law to take to court without exception for any person who violates the prohibition of closure, as well as violates sub-decrees and regulations."
In this audio message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that during the blockade of the capital and Takhmao city for the past two days, there were still people in traffic and congestion at each checkpoint. . Samdech Techo asked, "Where are they going?"
In this audio message, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also asked to check not to use the excuse that is a favorable case for travel to traffic in Phnom Penh and Takhmao. Samdech Techo also requested to check for the theft of people for travel from Phnom Penh by truck, this person or that ambulance.
Once again, Samdech Techo urged all citizens to work together to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and overcome the current national difficulties. Samdech Techo appealed, "Please try to bring our country back to its original state. "Otherwise, problems will continue to arise, which is difficult for our entire nation."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded the authorities to stand guard at each target to be careful of infection, especially to implement the rules to keep the gap.
On the night of April 14, the Royal Government issued a decision to close Phnom Penh and Takhmao City, banning people from leaving their homes or residences and suspending many businesses. Exemptions are required for travel with a specific specification and business related to food is also permitted.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that the blockade was not done to kill the people and the authorities were also ready to help the very poor. "We are not blocking the killing of the people, and the municipal authorities are ready to take action to rescue the poorest people," he said.
According to the Royal Government's decision, the permitted travel includes:
* Travel to work or conduct business or business in the geographical area of the block that is not prohibited as defined in Clause 3 and with attached documents confirming the work, occupation or business issued by the relevant business place or authority. Nearest land
* Travel to food or grocery stores and daily necessities authorized by the competent authority. Travel for this purpose may be carried out by a maximum of two (2) members per residence or lodge no more than three (3) times per week and at the nearest location within the geographical city or district. Living with a Khmer identity card or identity card
* Travel to appear for health officials to take samples for analysis of Kovid-19 and to be vaccinated against Kovid-19 on a regular basis and in or out of closed geographical circles
* Travel to participate in activities that serve the public interest or other necessary purposes upon request or as determined by the Public Works Authority.
Travel of diplomats, staff of foreign missions, UN agencies, international financial organizations, international organizations and foreign NGOs, along with identification and employment documents
* Travel in and out of the air-restricted area in accordance with the regulations and safety measures in force of health and travel for other necessary and urgent reasons, with the prior permission of the competent authorities that carry out the closed measures. Block.
In all of the above exceptions, everyone is obliged to implement health measures, including wearing a mask and keeping a safe distance, as well as adhering to sanitary and antiseptic measures to combat and prevent the spread of Kovid disease. 19.
The businesses licensed during this period include:
* Work activities of public institutions and the armed forces, but the head of the relevant institution must reduce the number of workers to a minimum to ensure the sustainability of the work of the institution. The head of the institution may decide to temporarily suspend unnecessary work as a matter of course.
* Factories, enterprises, handicrafts or places to produce food and groceries, including slaughterhouses, which are daily necessities.
* Work activities related to the provision of public services as determined by each institution, such as firefighting services, electricity supply, clean water, garbage collection and transportation services »solid waste, etc.
* All work, business or business activities that run online
* Supply of goods that are daily necessities, such as grocery stores, wholesalers, markets or grocery stores, orderly markets, marts and restaurants - restaurants that sell packaged food, gas stations, gas stations or supply locations that are Other daily necessities with the permission of the competent authority
* Provision of daily necessities such as emergency services, health and pharmacy services, postal-telecommunication services, banking and financial services and other daily necessities services with the permission of the competent authority. Reduce the number of employees to a minimum
* Hotel and Guesthouse Services
* Freight services required to serve a blocked geography
* General freight services in - out or through geographically blocked to serve the socio-economic sector of the country and
* Other necessary work, occupation or business activities with the permission of the competent authority.
All permitted activities, occupations or businesses as described above, everyone is obliged to implement health measures, including wearing a mask and keeping a safe distance, as well as adhering to hygiene, disinfection and temperature measurement. To fight and prevent the spread of Kovi 8-19.
