The provincial governor added that the emergency response team of the Department of Health will collect samples from all vendors on April 16, 2021 at the market in Sihanoukville. In case any trader fails to provide the sample as specified above, he / she must provide the sample at the forum on 7 January every working hour (including holidays).
At the same time, all traders and families must do the right thing at home in accordance with the instructions of the Ministry of Health.
The licensed trading businesses include the sale of foodstuffs (vegetables, fruits, fish, meat, spices, grains, rice, etc.) and vendors selling ready-made food (noodles, rice, noodles, porridge, noodles and all kinds of referrals); Selling drinks, but temporarily suspended for 3 days (16th, 17th and 18th) to spray disinfectant and clean the whole market.
The decision added that when food vendors had a negative Kovid 19 (first) certificate from the provincial health department, they could be allowed to resell, and the sale of ready-to-eat food and beverages could only be allowed. Must be packaged for customers.
Please be informed that as of the afternoon of April 16, 2021, 13 Phsar Leu traders have been diagnosed with 19 Kovid.
At the same time, the provincial administration will assign the Department of Commerce to monitor the prices of all kinds of goods sold on the market in Sihanoukville. If it is found that any trader is raising the price of goods incorrectly, the provincial administration will take the strictest administrative penalties, and if the increase in prices causes social unrest, the trader will face legal action without exception.
