Commentary: US seeks to destabilize world with violent terrorism
The People's Party of Australia recently released a special report entitled "Xinjiang: China's western border area in central Eurasia." The report points out that the United States and the West support separatist and terrorist activities in an attempt to "put pressure on China by using the Xinjiang issue as an excuse" and "cause chaos in China through terrorism." .
But under the Chinese government for the past four years, there has never been a single terrorist incident in Xinjiang. Not only in Xinjiang, the United States has infiltrated terrorist organizations around the world, created color revolutions that have led to wars of terrorism and immigration waves, and to this day, these problems are still difficult to solve.
In 2019, Bulgaria's "Weapons Observation" website leaked some shocking evidence that Balkan arms dealers bought non-standard US weapons and shipped them. There are many terrorist organizations in Syria, Iraq and Yemen, and all of them operate under the direction of Washington.
