(Singapore): In the sixth episode, you probably already know about the colonial events in Malaysia, and in the seventh episode, we would like to mention the colonial events in Singapore again, because Singapore, despite being a smaller country It is true, but it also leaves many traces of history in the colonial era.
* Pre-colonial Singapore
* Colonial Singapore
In 1511, the Portuguese colonized the kingdom of Malacca, including the territory of Singapore. By the 17th century, the Dutch had expelled the Portuguese from their base in Malacca, and in 1641 the monarchy had monopoly trade and political control over the kingdom of Malacca. At that time, the kingdom of Malacca had many small and large states, of which Joho was the largest state, dominating Singapore.
