Summary of the Royal Government's decision to close Phnom Penh and Takhmao for 14 days
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government has issued an urgent decision to block Phnom Penh and Takhmao for 14 days from zero on April 15 to April 28. During these 14 days, everyone is prohibited from leaving their current home or residence unless absolutely necessary. However, some necessary procedures are allowed.
* Allowed travel:
- Travel to work or do business or business in the geographical area of the block that is not prohibited as defined in Clause 3 and with attached documents confirming the work, occupation or business issued by the relevant business place or authority. Nearest land
Travel to places selling food or groceries and daily necessities that are authorized by the competent authorities. Travel for this purpose may be carried out by a maximum of two (2) members per residence or lodge no more than three (3) times per week and at the nearest location within the geographical city or district. Living with a Khmer identity card or identity card
Travel to appear before health officials for samples to be tested for Kovid-19 and to be vaccinated against Kovid-19 on a regular basis and in or out of enclosed geographies
- Travel to participate in activities that serve the public interest or other necessary purposes as requested or as determined by the Public Works Authority.
Travel of diplomats, officials of staff of foreign missions, UN agencies, international financial organizations, international organizations and foreign NGOs with identification and employment documents
Journalist's travel with identification documents and
* Businesses that allow to operate
During the implementation of the closure measures, all work activities, occupations or businesses that are not daily necessities are prohibited. However, work, occupation or business activities may be allowed in the following cases:
Work activities of public institutions and the armed forces, but the head of the relevant institution must reduce the number of workers to a minimum to ensure the sustainability of the work of the institution. The head of the institution may decide to temporarily suspend unnecessary work as a matter of course.
Factories, enterprises, handicrafts or places for the production of food and groceries, including slaughterhouses, which are daily necessities.
Work activities related to the provision of public services as determined by each institution, such as firefighting services, electricity supply, clean water, garbage collection and transportation services »solid waste, etc.
- All activities, occupations or businesses that operate through the online system
- Supply of goods that are daily necessities, such as grocery stores, wholesalers, markets or orderly food stalls, markets, markets and restaurants - Restaurants that sell packaged food, gas stations or supply locations Other daily necessities with the permission of the competent authority
- Supply of daily necessities such as emergency services, health and pharmacy services, postal-telecommunication services, banking and financial services and other daily necessities with the permission of the competent authority. Reduce the number of employees to a minimum
Hotel & Guesthouse Services
Freight services required to serve a blocked geography
- General freight services in - out or through geographically blocked to serve the socio-economic sector of the country and
- Other necessary work, occupation or business activities with the permission of the competent authority.
* Meetings allowed
During the implementation of the blockade measures, all gatherings or gatherings are prohibited. However, gatherings or gatherings of people may be allowed in the following cases:
Gatherings of family members living in the same house or shelter
Organizing funerals in accordance with the regulations of the competent authorities
Gatherings and meetings of health workers to implement health measures, such as taking samples to test for Kovid-19 and Kovid-19 vaccination, and meetings of health workers performing other emergency work; and
Gatherings of competent authorities, command forces, administrative units at all levels in the work of maintaining security, order and public order.
All authorized gatherings or gatherings, as described above, are the responsibility of the individual to implement health measures, especially the wearing of masks and gaps, as well as to adhere to hygiene to kill germs and Temperature measurements to combat and prevent the spread of Kovi 8-19, except for gatherings among family members living in the same house or shelter.
