The Ministry of Health would like to express its deepest condolences and condolences to the bereaved family. Ministry of Economy: Sub-decree on the implementation of value added tax on e-commerce is not a new tax
The reaffirmation comes after a misunderstanding that the newly enacted sub-decree on the implementation of value-added tax on e-commerce was a new taxation of the Royal Government of Cambodia, but it is true. No.
Mr. Kong Mary added that the General Department of Taxation has been studying the preparation of regulations on the implementation of value added tax on e-commerce, which is an initiative of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, for more than a year. Study visits and workshops in some countries to prepare all the regulations for implementation.
Please be informed that on April 13, 2021, the General Department of Taxation issued a press release stating that the Royal Government has decided to introduce VAT on digital goods and digital services supplied and used electronically by you. Supply of non-permanent residents in Cambodia.
The sub-decree on the implementation of value-added tax on e-commerce is not a new tax, but a strengthening of the implementation of the value-added tax provisions as stated in Article 75 of the tax law. Also in line with international standards.
In the past, value-added tax on e-commerce has not been implemented because there is no e-commerce law that clearly defines e-commerce, and according to this law, Doing business electronically is also a business, so taxpayers are obliged to pay taxes in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
On the other hand, this sub-decree was prepared in accordance with the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 and the Revenue Collection Strategy 2019-2023 of the Royal Government, as well as for the purpose of collecting revenue and strengthening tax transparency, as well as ensuring fair competition in Doing business in Cambodia.
At the same time, the implementation of this sub-decree can also attract more investment in the Kingdom of Cambodia in the field of information technology, which will drive the growth of this sector. With the General Department of Taxation, we strongly believe that enterprises and the national and international public will strive to strengthen the fulfillment of tax obligations in accordance with the laws and regulations on tax in force.
