As of the afternoon of April 14, 2021, the death toll from 19 cases of Kovid in Cambodia has risen to 35. Comment: China's foreign trade continues to grow sharply
BEIJING, April 13 (Xinhua) - The Chinese government on Tuesday released data on China's exports and imports in the first quarter, showing that the total volume of exports and imports of goods increased by 29 percent. 2% compared to the same period last year, in which exports increased by 38.7% and imports increased by 19.3%.
China's foreign trade performance in the first quarter has maintained a positive growth trend since the fourth quarter of 2020, which achieved a "good starting point" in 2021. The reasons for maintaining China's steady growth in foreign trade are not difficult to understand.
Exports can be seen that as the 199 Kovid vaccination framework has gradually expanded, the global economic recovery has shown positive trends. The World Trade Organization (WTO) recently raised its forecast for global trade in growth from 7.2 percent to 8 percent.
Improved external demand has strongly boosted China's exports. Imports show that China's manufacturing, investment and industrial consumption continue to recover, which has boosted imports. According to data released by the Chinese government, the recovery in manufacturing has pushed up imports of products such as integrated circuits and energy resources.
More importantly, China has effectively organized and managed the 19th Kovid disease prevention and control and economic development to provide strong support for the steady and continuous process of foreign trade. At the same time, from the trade score of foreign trade, the external environment has also seen the positive trend brought about by China's push for higher-level openness.
In the first quarter, the volume of exports and imports of China's mixed temporary customs area increased by 41.1%, the volume of exports and imports of the FTA area increased by 28.4% and the volume of duty-free imports of ports Hainan free trade rose 162.5 percent. It is clear that the higher level of openness has led to the growth of higher quality foreign trade.
