(Phnom Penh): Khmer New Year, which has been a Khmer tradition since ancient times, is the most meaningful time of the Khmer family, because this is the happiest time for people from all walks of life after being separated. To serve their respective causes, such as the national cause, the cause of family life and education, etc.
Unfortunately, this year is the second year that Cambodia and the Cambodian people have been harassed and harassed by Kovid 19, leading to a difficult decision by the Royal Government to block gatherings or travel to the district. Birth to celebrate the New Year, a happy time for Cambodians.
For the past two years, our entire Cambodian nation has not only been unable to celebrate its traditional festivals. But the Kovid 19 epidemic added another great burden and hardship for mankind: the fight for their livelihoods and well-being.
In the context of Kovid 19, we have made great efforts to ensure its operation and to contribute to the Royal Government in providing updates on the status of Kovid 19 and other social conditions. We have also put a lot of effort into fighting false news that misleads people and creates social stigma.
Despite the difficult time of the New Year celebration, the Cambodian people continue to celebrate this traditional celebration as far as possible according to the guidelines of the Royal Government and the authorities. Although it was not possible to reunite the family with the same celebrations as when Cambodia had not yet experienced Kovid 19, each family gathered as a small family to prepare various items to receive the New Year angels to receive the blessings of the year. New.
This New Year, I would also like to raise my hands and pray for the sacred objects in the world of Preah Ratanatray. To all types of armed forces who are standing to defend the territory and fulfill the mission in the cause of the motherland, be healthy, strong and successful in the mission to defend and serve the Cambodian nation.
I would also like to raise my hands and pray to the sacred objects in the world of Preah Ratanatray, with the Buddha, the Dharma, the monks as the chief deities, the guardian deities, the deities taking care of the whole universe by helping the governor to heal, nurture and bless everything. To the "White Army" medical team, which is working hard to fight Kovid 19 and save the lives of patients from Kovid 19.
In this new year, I would like to pray for the Cambodian nation to overcome Kovid 19 under the spirit of fighting together as a whole of the Cambodian people by listening to and following the instructions of the Royal Government as well as the relevant authorities. In particular, follow the health rules by adhering to the principles of "3 do not and 3 protect." Shoe seller at Chhouk Va 2 Market suffers from Kovid 19
