Phnom Penh Capital Hall Decides to Continue to Take Administrative Measures to Prevent Kovid Outbreak in Phnom Penh for Two More Weeks (Video inside) (Phnom Penh) Kovid in Phnom Penh for two more weeks from April 15 to 28, 2021.
The decision of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration states that:
* Suspended business activities for food stalls, restaurants, cafes, bars and restaurants in hotels, etc. Accepts customers to come and eat in their business premises, but can do business in the form of packaging.
* Suspended gatherings or gatherings for food, drink or alcohol between 8 pm and 5 am, except in the following cases:
Gatherings of family members living in the same residence or lodge - Organizing funerals in accordance with the authority's authority To carry Kovid-19 or to carry Kovid-19 as well as other emergency medical personnel
Meetings of the competent authorities, forces, command units, administrative units at all levels in the performance of work to maintain security, order and public order, gatherings of people who are necessary to serve the public interest or for other purposes as determined by the authorities. Competence.
* Traffic in Phnom Penh is temporarily suspended between 8pm and 5am, except in the following cases:
Travel for urgent health reasons and family necessities with a certificate or permit from the nearest competent authority
Travel of medical staff, both public and private, civil servants, firefighters, armed forces of all kinds to complete the mission to institutions - units
Traffic of Container Trucks, Trucks, Concrete Sprayers, Freight Forwarders, Construction Equipment, Construction Equipment, Trucks, and Solid Waste, Medical Waste
Transportation of food by staff, delivery service - Travel of staff and workers to the place of work in the enterprise, factory or business location that is allowed to open normally
Other necessary travel with the permission of the competent authority.
