Ramadan is the ninth month in the Islamic lunar calendar and is considered the lord of the other months. Because the lunar calendar year is 11 days shorter than the solar calendar, Ramadan revolves around each season. Example: Ramadan in 2020 is on April 24, while Ramadan in 2021 is on April 13 and it will continue to decrease every year.
In addition, this fasting is fasting during the forbidden time from dawn to dusk. During the day, one should not eat, drink or have sex, while a woman's menstruation also impairs fasting. However, unintentional or forgetful eating is not considered a break or damage to fasting.
