(World): Apart from the United States, the Indian subcontinent was also a delicacy for European colonists, who had been invading India since the late 15th century. It was not until 1947 that the great Asian nation regained its independence from Britain, but due to religious conflicts, Pakistan and Bangladesh seceded from India and continued on their own until today.
By 1858, all of India, as well as Burma, had come under British rule. From then on, India had no king to rule the country, and there was no retaliation against Britain, only silence for the next opportunity.
During World War I from 1914-1918 and World War II from 1939-1945, the United Kingdom mobilized large numbers of troops from India to go to war with their armies. The Indian Army, which was part of the British Army, played a key role in every battle in helping Britain fight the enemy.
After the victory of this independence claim, the Indian subcontinent was divided into two separate states due to religious conflicts, and Mahatma Gandhi was assassinated by extremist Hindus on January 30, 1948.
The departure of the United Kingdom left India and Pakistan in a state of conflict over Kashmir until the outbreak of a major war in 1971, which resulted in East Pakistan becoming another independent nation known as Kashmir. Bangladesh today.
