The National Bank of Cambodia sets out three principles for banking and financial institutions to implement to prevent the spread of Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): On April 12, 2021, the National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) issued a directive to all banking and financial institutions to implement three main principles to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
According to the instructions of the National Bank of Cambodia, in order to cooperate with the implementation of the measures of the Ministry of Health and measures to close the areas where there is a high epidemic of Kovid 19, the National Bank of Cambodia would like to recommend to all banking and financial institutions. As follows:
1. To temporarily suspend the operation of the branch or office in the closed area officially announced by the Royal Government or the local authority.
2. To inform the public clearly about the temporary suspension of operations at that branch or office and request customers to receive services at the nearest branch or office or operate through the online system of each banking and financial institution. . The notice shall be posted at the branch or office where the transaction is suspended and through various means such as social media and official website.
3. Maintain salaries and benefits for all employees who fail to work at the branch or office due to compliance with health measures, censorship and area closure measures.
This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation of Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on April 12, 2021.
During a video conference with Dr. Phorn Kham Viphavan, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his warmest congratulations to Dr. Phorn Kham Viphavan, the newly elected Prime Minister of the Lao People's Democratic Republic.
The Prime Minister expressed his belief that based on his great experience and strong leadership, the Lao People's Democratic Republic will achieve better socio-economic development and prosperity for the people of Laos.
The two prime ministers expressed their mutual appreciation for the close relationship based on traditional friendship and good neighborliness. The two leaders agreed to push for the speedy completion of the draft action plan for the partnership to further strengthen the close ties of cooperation in all fields, such as politics, security, trade, investment, education and culture.
The two leaders welcomed the increase in bilateral trade volume, which increased from 10 million US dollars in 2019 to 104 million US dollars by 2020. To boost investment in the two countries, the two leaders agreed to speed up negotiations on an "agreement to avoid double taxation".
Regarding the status of the Kovid-19 epidemic, the Prime Minister praised the Lao government's efforts to successfully control the Kovid-19 epidemic.
The Prime Minister of Laos expressed his sincere gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia for providing 2 million masks and some medical equipment to contribute to the fight against Kovid-19 in Laos.
The two prime ministers stressed the importance of strengthening cooperation to combat Kovid-19 and address the negative effects of the disease.
In addition to bilateral cooperation, the two leaders also exchanged views and pledged to work closely within the framework of multilateral cooperation. The Prime Minister thanked the Government of Laos for supporting Cambodia in hosting the 13th ASEM Summit at the end of 2021 and chairing ASEAN in 2022.
On the great occasion of the Khmer and Lao New Year, which will take place at the same time, the two Prime Ministers wished each other good health, prosperity and happiness to the people of Cambodia. And Laos. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Meets Video Conversation with New Lao Prime Minister Phorn Kham Viphavan
