Ms. Ly Lin also learned that the difficulty of this repair work is that the yard is small, difficult to move the stone and requires the use of human labor to move the stone. Therefore, the team used rubber mats on the pavement to place the stones, which moved to avoid direct contact with the stones, which could cause damage to the stone surface. On the other hand, if it rains or the rainy season arrives, it is difficult to repair.
The Khoeun structure on the third ridge of Bayon temple was damaged due to weather factors, trees, especially water leaking into the structure, which brought out the sand mixture, leading to problems at the corners, which could affect each other. To Khoeun Rout III and the whole temple construction as well.
Please note that this renovation project is carried out by experts of APSARA Authority, with technical cooperation between APSARA Authority and JASA Japan. After completing the project to repair the southwest corner, the team will continue to repair other high-risk areas and continue to study and repair other sites to maintain and strengthen the temple structure to be strong in the long run.
