Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit jointly give smiles to veterans in Pursat province by providing houses and land for accommodation and cultivation
(Pursat): 600 families of veterans who lack shelter and land for cultivation expressed their happiness after they received high attention and consideration from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kitti Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross.
At the request of Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Samdech Techo Hun Sen Veterans Association, it was decided to provide about 1.5 hectares of land in Say Village, Prongel Commune, Phnom Kravanh District, Pursat Province to build houses and cultivate crops. In addition, Samdech Kittipritthbandit provided funds to help build houses for them.
Currently, the Veterans Association and Pursat provincial authorities have deployed forces and machinery to clear land and build houses for veterans. On April 10, 2021, Senior Minister Kun Kim, Samdech Techo's personal staff on the work of the veterans, inspected the clearing and construction of this house.
Senior Minister Kun Kim told Fresh News that the land, villages and houses were directly managed and considered by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
The senior minister said there were about 600 families of veterans who would be living in the area. Each family was given 1.5 hectares of land as a policy regime for building houses and cultivating crops.
Separately, Samdech Kittipritthbandit helped to build houses for the veterans who face these needs. According to Senior Minister Kun Kim, in the first phase, Samdech Kittipritthbandit provided about $ 500,000 to build 164 houses. Currently, 26 houses have been completed, while 84 more will be completed soon. The remaining houses are scheduled for completion in May or June.
The senior minister also said that in addition to the process of clearing land and building houses, all relevant authorities are preparing to clear roads in the area, while the Ministry of Rural Development is helping to dig 10 wells with one house and will help build a road connecting The national road to the village of the newly created veterans as well.
During the visit to inspect the village for the veterans, Senior Minister Kun Kim warmly welcomed all the veterans. Senior Minister Kun Kim conveyed the greetings and greetings of Samdech Techo Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the families of all veterans.
The Senior Minister said that no matter what the circumstances, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always remember and think about the well-being, difficulties and shortcomings of veterans. Both Samdech always bring him and the leaders of the association, as well as the leaders of all capitals and provinces to pay attention, support and solve all problems and difficulties of the families of veterans.
The families of the veterans, who used to face hardships in their lives and lack housing to live in, have shown great excitement and enthusiasm for the compassion, kindness and consideration of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittiprittbandit.
They have always shown respect, love and support for Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who are the deities who walk on the ground for them. On that occasion, the veterans proposed to establish monasteries, health centers and schools for religious observance, easy access to health care and education for the children of the people.
For this request, Senior Minister Kun Kim promised to respect Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to review and decide. On that occasion, the Senior Minister continued to remind the leaders and authorities of Pursat province to pay attention and speed up the clearing of land, infrastructure and construction of houses for veterans to live and grow crops soon.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also did not forget to remind the families of all veterans to participate in health care together to fight the transmission and infection of Kovid 19 by following the health rules and recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen "3 do not and 3 protect " In addition, everyone must be vaccinated. Phnom Penh Authorities Implement Traffic Curf and Seize 3 More Motorbikes Last Night
