(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on the morning of April 11, 2021 issued a press release confirming the death of another 36-year-old Cambodian due to Kovid 19 disease.
On the morning of April 11, the Ministry of Health announced the death of 19 people from Kovid 19, a total of 3 people.
According to a statement from the Luang Mey Hospital, a 36-year-old Cambodian man living in Sambour village, Dangkor commune, Dangkor district, Phnom Penh, died of KD-19 on April 10, 2021 at 13:40.
Doctors' conclusion: The 36-year-old Cambodian man died of acute respiratory distress and pneumonia from the KV-19 virus. The Ministry of Health would like to express its deepest condolences and condolences to the bereaved family.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Health, as of this morning, April 11, 2021, a total of 29 people have died from 19 cases of Kovid. BREAKING: The Ministry of Health announces the deaths of two more Cambodian men and women due to Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of April 11, 2021, the Ministry of Health issued a press release on the deaths of two more Cambodian men and women due to Kovid 19 disease.
Case 1: According to a report from the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, a 48-year-old Cambodian man living in Prek Reang village, Kampong Samnang commune, Takhmao city, Kandal province, died on arrival at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital. On April 10, 2021 at 11:55 in the morning.
Upon arrival at the hospital on April 10, 2021 at 11:40 am, the patient was in a serious condition, fainted, lost consciousness, no signs of life, doctors helped to move the heart and provide technical assistance, but could not help. He was pronounced dead at 11:55 p.m. As a suspicion, the body was sampled by doctors and the result was confirmed to be positive Kovid-19.
Case 2: According to a report from Svay Chrum Referral Hospital in Svay Rieng Province, a 72-year-old Cambodian woman living in Prasop Lak Village, Bati Sangkat, Bavet City, Svay Rieng Province died of Kovid-19 on the 10th. April 2021 at 3:30 p.m.
The above patient was diagnosed with Kovid-19 on April 4, 2021 and was admitted to Svay Chrum Referral Hospital, Svay Rieng Province, but due to severe pneumonia and chronic diabetes mellitus. The body requires doctors to use a ventilator from the first day of hospitalization.
Despite medical efforts, doctors were unable to help and the patient's condition worsened, resulting in his death on April 10, 2021 at 3:00 p.m. 30 minutes in the afternoon.
Doctors' conclusion: The 72-year-old Cambodian woman died of severe lung failure and pneumonia from the Kovid-19 virus. The Ministry of Health would like to express its deepest condolences and condolences to the bereaved family.
