(World): In the 18th century, Europe began to have an industrial revolution, the new powers also expanded their colonies to find raw materials, expand markets, produce products and find a safe haven. Its shipping territories include Germany, the United Kingdom and France, as well as Russia.
2: The new superpower
For Britain, the Industrial Revolution was a major factor before the invasion of the colonies. They discovered the technology to build ships and steam-powered engines. Through this steamer, the British quickly sent troops from the capital, London, across the Atlantic to the Americas.
After James Cook's revelations, as well as many other sources, the British invaded India and colonized this vast country in 1858. Later, it colonized Malaysia and Singapore in 1826, colonized Hong Kong in 1841, Burma in 1885, and Brunei in 1888.
During the Republic, French troops arrived in Indochina in 1887 and subsequently colonized the Kingdom of Cambodia, the Kingdom of Tonkin, the Kingdom of Annam, and the territory of Cochinchina (Kampuchea Krom), Vientiane, Laos, and Yunnan Province of China. France mobilized troops from Cambodia, Cochinchina, and Annam to conquer colonies in several African countries, including Tunisia, Sudan, and Ivory Coast.
In the second half of the 19th century, French colonial politics faced many obstacles, such as the ridicule of the French people, especially the Socialist Party, and, in addition, the confrontation with the greed of other powers, including Britain. And Germany. However, thanks to the efforts of Jules Ferry, France was still able to expand its colonies enormously.
Before World War I, India and Southeast Asia fell under the yoke of European power almost entirely, with the exception of Siam, which was able to escape the clutches of the West thanks to the agreement of Britain and France. Together in 1896, leaving this empire as a buffer zone or "white" area between the colonies of the two powers.
The German Empire also gained control of parts of the Great Wall in 1897 and some territories in Africa. From 1839-1895, the Russian Empire invaded Central Asia and Turkey.
That is why in the 19th century, all the weakest countries in the world could not escape the oppression of the industrial powers.
