Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of delivering a special message to his compatriots regarding the situation of Kovid 19 in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at 9 am on April 10, 2021, delivered a special message to his compatriots regarding the situation of Kovid 19 disease in Cambodia.
* At the beginning of this morning's special broadcast, Samdech Techo Hun Sen shared his sadness with the families of all 19 victims of Kovid and greeted all the people who were receiving medical treatment.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if he did not take one step before the construction of the crematorium of Kovid 19 patients, he would not be able to control the situation. But Samdech thought one step ahead, despite the criticism that Samdech insulted people's lives.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the increase in the incidence of 19 Kovid patients in the February 20 community event was a bad event for Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised Vietnam and Thailand for managing community events well.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that measures to block 14 days of travel may not be enough, there may be further delays.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that the families of the 19 people who died of Kovid will pay for electricity at a reasonable rate for 5 months.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that the help of water and electricity to alleviate the hardships of the family.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that for families with 19 members of Kovid, the state will help pay for water and electricity at a reasonable level for three months from the day of Kovid 19 infection.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the state will provide 300,000 Riels per family and pay for water and electricity at the appropriate level for two months for families who have to do so in areas where the area is closed.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in addition to financial support and help with the cost of water and electricity, the state also provided 25 kilograms of rice, a small box of 20 cans of fish for the fishermen.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech will thank the families in the closed area and have a livelihood can solve the problem without the help of the state to reduce the cost of the state.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen appealed to Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), Private Water Supply Authority (PPWSA), private water companies to help supply the state for the families of 19 Kovid deaths and patients. Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that if not 100%, it should be a contribution.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the program to help solve this problem will be done throughout the country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this morning, Samdech ordered the Capital Governor to deliver food to the people in the blocked area with 300,000 Riels, Angkor noodles and canned fish.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Microfinance Association and the Banking Association for providing preferential payment of interest and principal for Kovid 19 patients.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that 340,000 people have been reorganized since the outbreak of Kovid 19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is not a planned market regime, so it is not possible to order the private sector to follow suit.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requests financial institutions and banks to waive interest and other penalties for 19-born Kovid and Chatsalysak:
1: For Kovid-19 infected customers: Exemption from interest payments and all fines for one month and automatic credit refinancing (if the client agrees) including deferment of principal payment For three months. All customers infected with Kovid-19 must present a positive Kovid-19 test result issued by the competent authority.
2: For customers who are engaged in debt consolidation: Provide automatic loan readjustment (if the customer agrees), including deferral of payment of both principal and interest for one month and waive all penalties.
3: Continue to provide credit restructuring quickly and conveniently for clients affected by Kovid-19.
4. Release emergency or supplementary loans by easing conditions and reducing interest rates to help continue and rehabilitate the family economy and business before and after the crisis.
6: Provide benefits for customers who have died of Kovid-19 according to the actual possibilities of each institution.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised Japan's attitude in finding all possible ways to help Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the Governor of Phnom Penh to confiscate vehicles for those who violate the curfew and to go home.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that today Samdech ordered to release 5 billion Riels for food intervention, you have to prevent them from leaving their homes.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the February 20 community event was a serious event for Cambodia, which led the Royal Government to take measures to close 19 Kovid explosions.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that no gatherings for eating, drinking or other events, including birthday parties.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Kovid 19 should not be trusted even by his relatives, only by himself.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Khmer New Year is still held but must be held at home. Especially at New Year at home, ensure safety from Kovid 19 disease.
