According to Minister Thong Khon, the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation has sent a letter from the European Union (EU) and the Spanish Ministry of Foreign Affairs on the entry into force of the revised World Tourism Organization (WTO) statute, which became Chinese. The official language of the World Tourism Organization on January 25, 2021.
At the meeting on the approval of Chinese as the 6th official language of the World Tourism Organization was held at the General Assembly of the World Tourism Organization on November 29, 2007 in Colombia. Member States are required to provide support by sending official letters of support to the EU Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Spanish Cooperation.
According to the World Tourism Organization's charter, the official use of the Chinese language by the World Tourism Organization requires the support of two-thirds of the 159 member states.
At the same time, 106 member states of the World Tourism Organization have sent letters of support for the official use of the Chinese language by the World Tourism Organization (WTO) by providing final direct support to be completed by January 25, 2021, including Cambodia. Letters of support have already been sent since 2012.
On behalf of Cambodia, a member state of the World Tourism Organization, the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia is also preparing a letter of congratulations to the Chinese Ministry of Culture and Tourism and the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia to celebrate the Chinese language. Official of the World Tourism Organization.
