Commentary: Chinese heroes in the fight against the spread of Kovid 19 help Wuhan find a way to solve this crisis
On April 8, 2020, Wuhan officially lifted measures to close the gates to Wuhan and Hubei provinces. April 8, 2021 is the one-year anniversary of the abolition of the city and province closure measures. It is one of the most courageous measures to prevent and control infectious diseases in human history, and it is also an unprecedented voluntary sacrifice that demonstrates China's obligations and responsibilities.
In the fight against the epidemic for 76 days, the international community has focused on China, and China has focused on Wuhan. According to statistics, regions across China have deployed a total of more than 30,000 medical personnel to help Wuhan, and areas have accelerated the production of all kinds of medical equipment to supply and transport to Wuhan. Timely.
More than 3,000 communities, more than 7,000 residents and more than 13,800 networks have been fully operational, and more than 40,000 party cadres, party members and staff in Wuhan have worked in the community under Lead of community cadres. Community volunteers worked hard day and night everywhere, becoming the city's conservators.
The city of Wuhan, which was closed for 76 days due to the outbreak of Kovid 19 and under severe pressure, has begun a speedy recovery after overcoming the epidemic. Rehabilitation factories, schools reopened, supermarkets and restaurants reopened, Wuhan has been bustling in the past.
As the spread of infectious diseases across China has been better managed, more than 400 top national and international enterprises, more than 400 enterprises, have traveled to Wuhan to observe and discuss Trading. In 2020, Wuhan mobilized more than 930 billion yuan in actual investment, up 6.7 percent from 2019.
At the same time, China's first 5G Plus Internet Industry Conference was held in Wuhan to promote the rapid development of the digital economy. High-tech enterprises have set up offices in Wuhan's Tonghu New Technology Development Zone to help build China's National Technology Innovation Center.
Wuhan has been embracing new occupational formulas and new opportunities created during the epidemic to promote formula change and promote the traditional industrial hierarchy. Wuhan's total economic size by 2020 will exceed 1.5 trillion yuan, once again becoming the top 10 cities in China.
Individual efforts have helped Wuhan find opportunities in crisis and pioneered new developments in a context of change. In a context where Kovid 19 is still prevalent around the world, the global economy is being hit hard.
China, as the world's only major economic entity, has achieved positive growth. Faces can not be separated from the support and efforts of all Chinese people. The heroes who fight infectious diseases are all of us.
As spring arrives with sakura blossoms all over Wuhan, we welcome you from far away to visit Wuhan to taste the Michigan, see the cherry blossoms and climb the ancient Huang Helou. The people there will be warm and welcoming, and Wuhan will be much safer.
