Mr. Vongsy Visoth said that Cambodia was facing an outbreak of Kovid-19 at the February 20 community event, which had led to a steady increase in the number of cases and deaths. He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia considers preventing the spread of Kovid 19 virus as a top priority.
In fact, since the first outbreak of Kovid 19, the Royal Government has always paid close attention and given the highest priority to:
* First: the fight against Kovid-19 to prevent infection and protect the lives of the people * Second: to maintain the balance of life, especially for the poor, vulnerable and unemployed * 3. Efforts are made to help businesses and businesses survive and maintain jobs, especially the maintenance and promotion of local economic activity * Fourth: Maintaining security, public order, social stability and economic and financial stability .
At the same time, Cambodia also started the Kovid-19 vaccination program in accordance with its vaccination and procurement plans. To date, Cambodia has received 3,124,000 doses of the vaccine and vaccinated the population. More than 800,000 people, which is about 8% of the target population of about 10 million people.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth also said that within the framework of the Cambodian Economic Recovery Plan after the Kovid-19 crisis, the Royal Government has allocated about 1.16 billion US dollars in 2020 (of which about 829 million Dollars have already been provided) and more than 719 million US dollars in 2021.
Meanwhile, the Royal Government of Cambodia is preparing to launch a plan for economic recovery after the Kovid-19 crisis 2021-2023, focusing on three approaches, including:
The meeting reviewed and evaluated the progress of the implementation of the health, social assistance, and economic support programs of the Kovid-19 Epidemic and Economic Rehabilitation (CARES) program.
The meeting also discussed some issues in the implementation of the program raised by the relevant ministries and institutions, such as the possibility of access to credit of the private sector, which is still a major issue, which has a significant impact on e-promotion. COMMERCE, the key to Cambodia's economic recovery and reform measures to help the industry recover and Big Data.
