(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Economy and Finance on April 9, 2021, issued a joint proclamation on intermediate penalties for individuals who do not comply with administrative measures to prevent Kovid 19 and other serious and dangerous diseases. Other.
According to Article 1 of the Inter-Ministerial Prakas, transitional penalties for individuals who do not comply with administrative measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and other serious and dangerous diseases are the responsibility of the sub-national administration.
Article 2 states that individuals who intentionally fail to comply with administrative measures shall be subject to a transitional fine of 1 million to 5 million riels, regardless of other criminal offenses.
The amount of the penalty for the transitional penalty according to each administrative measure for the person who does not intentionally comply with the administrative measures shall be decided by the relevant Capital / Provincial Administration.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of April 9, 2021, the last day of the Kovid-19 vaccination campaign (first dose) at the General Secretariat of the National Assembly for the leadership and officials of the framework and contracted officials of the General The Secretariat of the National Assembly, which started the seven-day process from April 3 to 9, 2021, on a voluntary basis.
Mr. Leng Peng Long, Secretary General of the National Assembly, on behalf of the civil servants of the Secretariat of the National Assembly, thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Ministry of Health, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, for paying close attention to the well-being of the civil servants of the Secretariat of the National Assembly. Which allowed doctors to come and vaccinate all 19 civil servants at the National Assembly directly.
According to the Secretary General of the National Assembly, from the day of the vaccination process from the 3rd to the 9th of April 2021, which is the last day, the families of the leaders of the National Assembly and civil servants of the General Secretariat of the National Assembly volunteered to come. A total of 1,328 people received 19 vaccines.
Mr. Leng Penglong also instructed all civil servants of the General Secretariat of the National Assembly to continue to maintain good health, even after the first dose of vaccination, must continue to implement the "3 prevent 3" measures, as well as the Royal Guidelines. The government and the Ministry of Health must not be negligent.
"Vaccines are very important today in protecting people's lives and improving the socio-economic situation after the Kovid-19 pandemic," he said.
The Royal Government plans to vaccinate 10 million people out of a total population, and in this large-scale campaign, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has instructed the Ministry of Health to vaccinate one million doses per month.
Once again, the Secretary-General of the National Assembly expressed his deep gratitude to the team of volunteer doctors and all relevant officials who worked hard to provide the first dose of Kovid 19 vaccine at the General Secretariat of the National Assembly with high responsibility. Until completed successfully. He also handed out leaflets and souvenirs to the volunteer doctors.
Please be informed that for the second dose of Kovid 19 vaccine to the civil servants of the General Secretariat of the National Assembly, the Ministry of Health will inform the time later.
