Chinese Human Rights Research Association publishes article on US foreign war of aggression poses serious humanitarian disaster
BEIJING (Reuters) - The Chinese Association for the Study of Human Rights published an article entitled "US foreign aggression war causes serious humanitarian catastrophe", citing examples of some US-inspired war of aggression after World War II. The second is to expose the atrocities of the United States, using "humanitarian intervention" as an excuse to incite wars of aggression.
The article analyzes in depth that these wars not only claimed many lives but also caused many civilian deaths and injuries, as well as severe property damage, causing serious humanitarian catastrophe. .
According to incomplete statistics cited in this article, from the end of World War II to 2001, out of 248 armed clashes in 153 regions around the world, the United States was the instigator. Up to 201 times.
The article revealed that the military operation led to a humanitarian crisis that originated from the idea of American hegemony. Expecting a country to adopt pro-political policies to protect the human rights of other countries is as instructive as asking for tiger skins. As long as the idea of self-serving practice can be abandoned, then the people of other countries can enjoy basic human rights.
