Every year in the spring, several large ships leave Lisbon, the capital of the Portuguese Empire, and in the fall they return to the port of Lisbon, loaded with spices and pepper. Silk, linen, precious stones, fragrant wood and rosewood, as well as porcelain. This exclusive trade in the East brought huge profits to Portugal.
People living in Portuguese-dominated areas often had to become Christians through the preaching of Catholic priests as well as coercion by their governors, and all mosques had to become Catholic. . All the ports of trade from Africa to the east, which were once Arab destinations, were replaced by the Portuguese.
In South America in the 16th century, the Portuguese colonized what is now Brazil and brought slaves from Africa to work in agriculture and gold mining.
That is why there was a mixture of race between the Europeans, the natives and the blacks to form the Latin American people as they are today.
