Nearly 5,000 Veterans Vaccinated on First Day of Campaign, Veterans Happy to Be Vaccinated
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Veterans Association on Thursday, April 08, 2021, launched the Kovid 19 Sinovak vaccination campaign for veterans across the country. The first day of the campaign involved vaccinating 19 Kovid on 19 veterans in nine provinces, and 4,719 fighters have already been vaccinated.
Reports show that the capitals and provinces that vaccinated 19 Kovid vaccines today include Phnom Penh, Kandal, Pursat, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear, Kampong Thom and Stung Treng.
General Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Veterans Association, who is the personal secretary of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen, personally inspected the vaccination of veterans. Senior Minister Kun Kim, in addition to inspecting the injections in Kandal province, also visited Oddar Meanchey and Kampong Thom provinces.
The staff, which was trusted by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Mr. Kun Kim emphasized during the inspection of the vaccination process that on the first day, the vaccination was done in only 9 capitals and provinces, and tomorrow the vaccination will be conducted in other provinces. More. According to him, the injection will be completed in the near future.
Through Fresh News, Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked the 25 Capital-Provincial Governors as well as all the leaders of the Veterans Association for their diligence in facilitating the vaccination of veterans.
The Kovid 19 vaccine is a new tool in addition to existing medical measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and save lives by helping individuals avoid severe illness when infected with Kovid 19 and reducing hospitalization.
Senior Minister Kun Kim highlighted Samdech Techo Hun Sen's great concern in protecting the lives of citizens and veterans in order to avoid the devastating 19 communicable diseases that are occurring in Cambodia.
Veterans also see the value of vaccines in protecting their health and lives from the Kovid 19 pandemic. Veterans have all expressed satisfaction and joy in getting vaccinated without any loneliness or belief in any unfortunate incitement.
Veterans also took this opportunity to express their deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who are always very caring and caring for veterans.
