(Siem Reap): Peanut Lake is a natural tourist area with many rare fish and birds that can attract tourists to visit in large numbers. Due to the Kovid 19 crisis, boat owners lost their daily income from bird watching, and they complained about the impact on their livelihoods.
Un Pheara, a member of the Peanut Lake Ecotourism Community, said there were nine tourist boats in the area and divided into two groups. Tourists who come here enjoy boating, watching the flooded forest and watching many kinds of birds, especially in the dry season.
Under these circumstances, not many tourists come to visit Peanut Lake, which is more than 10 kilometers from the town of Siem Reap. Today's visit is only for tourists in the province who come as a family and pack food. Mr. Phara added that the sales are not very good because most of the guests who come are mostly packed food from home.
