Commentary: Targeted Poverty Alleviation needs to find the right way
(Beijing): Poverty is multifaceted and hardship is multifaceted. Targeting poverty eradication, that is, finding out the real causes of poverty and ensuring specific poverty alleviation and real efforts.
At that crucial time, on the occasion of the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China, 100 million poor people under the current standard line have lifted themselves out of absolute poverty, achieving the goal of reducing poverty. According to the United Nations 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development, 10 years before the end of the year, China's poverty alleviation campaign has been successful in all aspects.
Why China Can Achieve Outstanding Global Poverty Alleviation Achievement Strategies aimed at eradicating poverty play an irreplaceable role. It can be said that targeted poverty alleviation is the "password" for successful poverty alleviation work.
With regard to the number of poor people, the level of poverty and the causes of poverty in poor areas, etc., the Chinese government has planned according to different situations in different regions and will implement policies aimed at eradicating poverty. Much like helping to eradicate poverty through science and technology, education, e-commerce, tourism and finance.
While China has accomplished the task of overcoming poverty in a timely manner, the living standards of the people who have escaped poverty have also been remarkably improved. Not all. Overcoming obstacles to eradicate poverty is important to be targeted and whether or not success can be achieved through targeted implementation.
As poverty eradication campaigns become more successful in the region, the meaning and impact of poverty eradication campaigns are spreading abroad. In recent years, China-Cambodia Poverty Alleviation Assistance Project has made steady progress, and China's experience in reducing poverty has benefited Cambodia's rural areas.
Kem Rath Viseth, President of the Cambodian Civil Society Forum, said that the Chinese government and civil society organizations of China have provided invaluable and in all possible ways to Cambodia, which has brought tangible benefits to economic and social development in Cambodia. Area.
In particular, since the Chinese-sponsored technical assistance project to reduce poverty in Cambodia began in Svay Ampear and Chheuteal Phlos villages, Svay Ampear commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province, taking into account the actual situation in the region, Chinese experts Encouraged villagers with land to grow mushrooms.
Cambodia is in the tropics, so growing mushrooms in high temperatures can yield three seasons a year and can be very lucrative. The experts also arranged for the villagers to set up two dishwashing soap factories in the form of a shareholding of their land.
The two factories can now produce 50,000 bottles of dishwashing soap a year, and the annual output can reach $ 15,000. In particular, to solve the problem of drinking water, experts have organized the villagers to build water towers, dig water wells and lay water pipelines, so that nearly 4,000 villagers can use clean water.
Truth is not alone, the whole world is one great family. China's successful implementation of poverty reduction has not only enriched people across China, but also provided new options for some countries in the world. Want to get development fast too.
Nine lawyers volunteer to defend security in Teuk Thla flyover
