Ministry of Environment instructs provincial environment departments to implement effective measures to close ecotourism destinations to prevent Kovid-19
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has issued instructions to environmental departments in all provinces targeting protected areas and biodiversity corridors to implement high-quality and responsible temporary closure measures.
According to the instruction received by Fresh News on April 8, 2021, the issuance of this instruction came after the Royal Government decided to ban travel and close tourist resorts throughout the country. Temporarily to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
The directive states that all provincial departments of environment must cooperate with provincial administrations, units and relevant local authorities to temporarily close tourist resorts, tourism communities and tourist destinations within protected areas and biodiversity corridors for 14 days from From zero hours on April 7 to April 20, 2021 in order to fight and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
At the same time, it is necessary to cooperate in monitoring and prohibiting all entry-exit travel and not to allow any tourism service activities at tourist destinations in protected areas and biodiversity corridors during the temporary closure. This is absolute.
According to Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, the Ministry of Environment has been protecting and conserving 74 protected areas and biodiversity corridors covering a total area of 7.3 million hectares. Approximately 41% of the land area of Cambodia is located in 21 provinces of Cambodia, while Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Cham, Svay Rieng do not have protected areas.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that in these protected areas and biodiversity corridors, there are some areas with tourism potential, including 26 ecotourism communities have been invested and developed many ecotourism sites and tourist destinations. Many more in protected areas.
These tourist sites include: Kirirom Tourist Resort, Kampong Speu Province, Phnom Kulen, Siem Reap Province, Chrakleang Waterfall, Pursat Province, Chi Phat Ecotourism Community, Koh Kong Province, Busra Waterfall, Mondulkiri Province, Boeung Yak Loam, Boeung Lamkud, Ratanakkiri Province.
The following is the instruction of the Ministry of Environment: Send the killer of a 10-year-old boy in Chbar Ampov district to court to be punished according to the law
(Phnom Penh): The Criminal Police of Chbar Ampov District Inspectorate, Phnom Penh, on the morning of April 8, 2021, sent the killer of a 10-year-old boy to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for processing.
It should be reminded that after the body of the victim boy was found in a lake forest along Tiger Road in Boang Kanh 1 Village, Sangkat Prek Eang, Khan Chbar Ampov, the specialized police force immediately opened the search until the night of April 5. In 2021, the perpetrator was arrested at Chroy Ampil pagoda in Chroy Ampil village, Sangkat Kbal Koh, Khan Chbar Ampov for questioning.
After receiving a confession that he killed the victim boy because he was angry, his grandmother-in-law hit him on the head once and forbade him to listen. At noon on April 6, 2021, the specialized police force brought the perpetrator back to the scene to simulate the act of killing his nephew. Authorities confirmed that the assailant was On Phamon, 31, a resident of Kbal Koh commune, Chbar Ampov district.
The operation was carried out under the direct command of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, and was directed by Lt. Gen. In Bora, Deputy Commissioner for Planning, and Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner and Capital Police Commissioner. Phnom Penh and Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, Director of the Criminal Police Department.
During the search operation until the crackdown on the perpetrators on April 5, 2021 by the force of the Criminal Police Department led by Major General Cheav Vibol, Deputy Director of the Department in collaboration with the Police Inspectorate of Chbar Ampov District, Serious Criminal Police Office Of Phnom Penh Police and CPU.
A 10-year-old boy went missing on March 31, 2021 and was found dead in the forest on April 2, 2021, along Tiger Street. Bao Angkanh 1 village, Sangkat Prek Eang, Khan Chbar Ampov, suspected of murder. The victim was identified as Chea Bunheng, a resident of Chroy Ampil village, Kbal Koh commune.
Witnesses confirmed to the family that they saw the child victim riding a motorcycle taxi before disappearing. Later, the information was given to the authorities, only to find that the boy had been killed.
