Police send police officer who shot a drug dealer with a knife to stab himself in court this morning
(Phnom Penh): The criminal police force of Sen Sok District Inspectorate this morning, April 8, 2021, sent the police officers guarding ABA Bank under Phsar Dei Huy flyover to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. In that case, the officer fired at the detainee while holding a knife, chased and stabbed him in order to protect himself, and caused the detainee to lose his life at the scene.
Inspector Ho Meng Wang confirmed that the police officer currently resides at 57E1, Street 118, Sangkat Phsar Thmei I, Khan Daun Penh. He shot Ou Sopharat, a 27-year-old homeless man, in Room 104, Concrete Road, Phsar Teuk Thla Village, Sangkat Teuk Thla, Khan Sen Sok (methamphetamine), and died at the scene.
Materials left as evidence include a sharp knife of the deceased, 1 original Macrolo pistol, number 3388, black wood, 4 shells of the suspect.
However, the public on Facebook expressed support for the actions of a police officer guarding the ABA Bank who shot the man to death because he had used violence against the police and eventually ran for more knives. Only then did the police officer decide to detonate his weapon. The action was clearly filmed by security cameras.
Distributed security camera footage showed two gangsters initially chasing each other on the street, and one of the gangsters who was chased ran to a nearby ABA Bank security guard (one of the above police officers) to Intervene. At that time, the perpetrator became very angry with the police officer guarding and security and also used violence against the police.
Although the police officer shot and killed the perpetrator, the public believed that the shooting was only to protect themselves from the perpetrator's stabbing, there was no intention to shoot to kill, because from the first incident, officers The police did not retaliate against the perpetrators.
It is presumed that the police officer shot to protect himself because after the incident caused the death of the perpetrator, the police officer did not escape from the scene and agreed to surrender to the authorities. Therefore, it is hoped that the prosecution will consider the legal aspect to drop the charges against the police officer.
