(Mondulkiri): Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Mondulkiri Province, on April 7, 2021, together with the three forces and the relevant departments and units, the district authorities inspected the target of the authorities to ban the transit from From one province to another at the border between the two provinces in Koh Nhek and Keo Seima districts to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
On that occasion, Mr. Svay Sam Eang said that the inspection of the feet of the authorities now aimed at encouraging the authorities to tighten the implementation of the decision of the Royal Government to be more effective.
The Governor of Mondulkiri Province instructed the District Unity Command to ban the gathering of various ceremonies, including ceremonies at pagodas, and instructed the resorts to suspend business temporarily. Immigrants are required to have a 14-day vaccination program at home or at a proper vaccination center to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in Mondulkiri province.
The provincial governor said that the ban on people traveling from one province to another is to prevent the spread of Kovi 19 from one area to another, from one province to another, especially the Royal Government for health. The public takes into account the lives of the people and the society.
Mr. Svay Sam Eang also requested all people to participate in implementing the measures of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health to protect themselves from the transmission of Kovid 19.
The provincial governor also brought some materials to support the forces standing at the above two targets, including: rice, noodles, pure water, orange juice, alcohol, a budget of 2 million riels per target. Separately, General Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, donated 1 million Riels to the police stationed in Koh Nhek district through the provincial commissioner.
