Situation in Myanmar: "Seven killed in Wednesday crackdown, another Chinese factory set on fire"
Security forces opened fire on protesters in the northwestern city of Kale on Wednesday, leaving five people dead and several others injured, local media reported. In Bago, near Rangoon, two other protesters were also shot dead.
On the same day, a Chinese garment factory in Rangoon was set on fire, but there were no reports of injuries or damage. Last month, 32 Chinese factories were set on fire in Rangoon.
Since the unrest erupted in early February, according to Human Rights Watch in Myanmar, a total of nearly 600 people have been shot dead by Myanmar police and soldiers almost daily. . Nearly 3,500 people have been arrested, of whom 2,750 have yet to be released.
