The letter stated that in order to follow the advice of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Ministry of Public Service would like to immediately request the provision of the number of civil servants and contracted officials of the Ministry, institutions, administrative units, capitals and provinces (excluding troops). Armed Forces) which has not been vaccinated against Kovid-19 as of April 11, 2021.
According to the letter, according to the letter, please kindly quote the number of civil servants and contracted officials according to the attached list sample and send it immediately to the Ministry of Public Function before April 11. 2021 to summarize and respect Samdech Techo Hun Sen in a timely manner.
On the evening of April 6, 2021, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, issued a special message announcing that in the future, the Armed Forces and civil servants who avoid vaccinating against Kovid 19 may Will lose his job immediately.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's announcement came after he received a report that after the Royal Government launched a series of vaccination campaigns for the armed forces and civil servants, there are two types of officials: first, those who want to be vaccinated. Be quick to defend yourself and another as an officer who avoids not wanting to be vaccinated.
"It is true that the vaccine is given on a voluntary basis, but in the future it is clear that the vaccine will become a mandatory vaccine, especially in the first step, in our armed forces and our civil servants," he said. All.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked all ministries and units to monitor the officers under their command, the army as well. Samdech also instructed provincial and district governors to monitor officials in their provinces who have not been vaccinated if officials who intentionally missed them should not be allowed to work.
Samdech Techo praised the army led by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, who so far almost 100 percent of the army has injected the first dose and about 70 to 80 percent. Second. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also encouraged Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara to push for more vaccinations by allowing cleaners and gardeners to be vaccinated.
"This is a public health issue, a voluntary issue, but we need to think about the common interest of the nation about public health," he said.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also warned against collusion between doctors and officials who intend not to vaccinate. Samdech continued that in order to avoid collusion between doctors and those who intend not to be vaccinated, all vaccinators must have a specific certification from the specialized unit. Samdech continued that in the future, if possible, in addition to the card provided by the health department, we may have a badge to identify those who have been vaccinated by the relevant ministry.
Samdech appealed that those who intend not to be vaccinated are more likely to lose their jobs in the armed forces, both at the national and sub-national levels, and contracted officials. However, Samdech warned that it is not too late for the officials to be vaccinated.
