A 7-month-pregnant woman who squeezed the victim's mouth, stuffed it with paper, injected 502 glue and removed a necklace from a family feud two years ago
After sleeping for a while, an unidentified person squeezed the victim's mouth, stuffed it with paper towels and put 502 glue into the victim's mouth while the victim was sleeping on a hammock, causing the victim Unable to speak, the suspect removed the necklace from one of the victims and fled.
Until April 6, 2021, the police force investigated and found the suspect, Kun Houch, female, 28 years old, in Ta Som village, Ta Som commune, Angkor Chum district, Siem Reap province. The suspect confessed that he actually took 502 glue, put it in the victim's mouth and stole the necklace that the victim was wearing. The reason he committed this crime was because of out of family resentment two years ago.
