Siem Reap Provincial Administration Closes Cross-Provincial Traffic
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Administration on the morning of April 7, 2021 has started to implement the Royal Government's directive prohibiting travel in and out of the province.
Mr. Nak Neron, Deputy Governor and Chairman of the Task Force to Investigate and Monitor Suspected People with Kovid-19 in Siem Reap Province, confirmed that the Chi Kreng District Authority, which is adjacent to Kampong Thom Province, has started to carry out its work under the guidance of the Provincial Unity Command. And according to the decision of the Royal Government to close traffic from one province to another from April 7 to 20.
The deputy governor, who inspected the arrangement, confirmed that the authorities did not allow entry into the province, except in cases of necessity, such as hospitalization, in case of a mission letter. Ordinary citizens are not allowed in or out.
According to Mr. Nak Neron, the situation on the border of Siem Reap and Kampong Thom is not a problem because people have received comprehensive information and participate in the implementation of this decision.
