General Vong Pisen Introduces Preparation for Lightweight Kovid-19 Patients in Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Institutional Units
The directive states that in accordance with the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in the fight against Kovid-19, which is spreading in the community, the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) Under the General Command as follows:
1: Set up a treatment center for Kovid-19 patients at the perimeter of each unit, equipped with beds and some necessary medical equipment.
2: Prepare the health force and prepare to train the doctors to care for and treat the low-level Kovid-19 patients in their unit.
3: Continue to set up separate locations for units in the unit to conduct soldiers who are suspected of being involved with Kovid-19 patients.
4: Soldiers who have not been vaccinated against Kovid-19 must immediately be vaccinated at designated locations, except for soldiers who have a medical condition and a doctor has issued a permit not to vaccinate. In front of all military bases, any soldiers who have not been vaccinated and are not allowed to enter the military base must be inspected.
