(Phnom Penh): The new Prime Minister of Vietnam, Mr. Pham Minh Chinh, expressed his commitment to continue to work closely and closely with the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen to continue to strengthen good neighborly relations, traditional friendship and cooperation. Every corner.
The assertion of the new Prime Minister of Vietnam was made in a telephone conversation with Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the afternoon of April 6, 2021, during which the Prime Minister expressed his warmest congratulations to him. Pham Minh Chinh was elected Prime Minister by the 11th session of the 14th National Assembly.
The two sides agreed to effectively carry out border management, fight cross-border crime, cooperate in preventing the spread of Kovid 19, promote trade exchanges and timely resolve any issues that may arise. The two sides agreed to continue to work closely within the framework of multilateral cooperation.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the great achievements of the Vietnamese people so far and expressed confidence that under the wise leadership of Pham Minh Chinh, the Vietnamese government and people will successfully implement Five-year socio-economic development plan (2021-2025) and 10-year economic development strategy (2021-2030) through the decisions of the Communist Party and the National Assembly of Vietnam.
Mr. Phan Minh Chinh thanked Cambodia for successfully supporting Vietnam in its ASEAN Chairmanship in 2020 and reaffirmed Vietnam's support for Cambodia in hosting the Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM). ) 13th time at the end of 2021 and chair of ASEAN in 2022 successfully.
