Ms. Mom Chandani said that in response to the humanitarian action to prevent anyone from dying without food or because our authorities do not know, while the Department of Social Affairs inspected and asked them to return. Take shelter and enter the house to protect them from the risk of the February 20 community event wave that has been spreading in the community.
At the same time, Mr. Touch Channy also stated that the vulnerable group does not want to live in the center where the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Social Affairs has taken them to live under the care and upbringing of the national policy. He wants to live freely, wandering the streets at traffic lights to live one of their kind.
Regarding the prevention of Kovid 19 disease, Mr. Touch Channy confirmed that today, the Department of Social Affairs has many centers that take people to centers such as mental health centers, orphanages, homeless people, and these centers have a high risk, so the team visited Distribute alcohol-gel masks and strengthen instruction to teach them to wear hand-washing masks and alcohol-gel soaps to protect themselves from Kovid 19.
Mr. Toch Chanini added that as a measure to protect Kovid 19 during the New Year, we do not allow outsiders to enter and leave the center. Ministry of Labor issues Prakas on the use of transport permits for workers and work during travel restrictions in order to prevent the spread of Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor issued a Prakas on the use of permits to transport workers and work during travel restrictions in order to prevent the spread of Kovid 19. This is according to the announcement that Fresh News received on the night of April 6, 2021.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has informed the owners or directors of factories that are not designated to close business activities, workers and employees, and drivers or owners of means of transportation of workers and employees as follows:
A: For workers and staff
* Users of personal and solo means of transportation must bring a worker or employee ID card and a Cambodian identity card or other document proving their current address on each trip to and from work. House to present to the competent authorities
* Users of public transportation must ride a vehicle with a "worker transport permit" issued by the Ministry or the Department of Labor and Vocational Training and carry the identity card of workers and staff with them every time they travel to work and Return home to present to the competent authorities.
B: To the owner or director of the enterprise
* Must provide a list of license plates, vehicles or means of transportation to the Labor Inspector.
* Must cooperate with the Labor Inspector to provide the "Worker Transport Permit" to the driver (as attached) for presentation to the competent authorities when transporting workers and staff to the workplace and back home.
* Ensure that all workers and employees have an ID card. In case of disappearance, ID card must be issued to workers and employees immediately.
C: For drivers or owners of means of transportation, workers and staff
* Must obtain a "worker transport permit" from the factory and must be displayed on the front of the means of transportation to present to the competent authorities.
