Samdech Techo Hun Sen Introduces Increased Vaccination in Phnom Penh and Kandal Provinces
(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has instructed the Kovid 19 Vaccination Commission to make plans for the next vaccination, increasing vaccinations in Phnom Penh and Kandal. The national road from Phnom Penh has a lot of workers. For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, increase vaccination in Phnom Penh and Kandal province to increase immunity for people in Phnom Penh and Kandal province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also revealed clues about identifying people to be vaccinated. According to Samdech Techo, vaccinations for priority people have already been done, so the next vaccine will be given to all individuals of all ages and health conditions in accordance with the vaccination requirements.
In the past, Cambodia has set the principle of voluntary vaccination. But to develop immunity, vaccination can become mandatory, no longer on a voluntary basis.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that those who do not get vaccinated may find it difficult to find work and may also become discriminated against by vaccinators.
Samdech Techo confirmed this issue as follows: "Soon in the world, vaccines can become a mandatory vaccine, this is my expectation. "I think those who have not been vaccinated are the unfortunate ones who have not been able to get a job or have been welcomed by those who have been vaccinated, which creates discrimination."
Apart from the geography in Phnom Penh and Kandal Province, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed the Commission for discussions with Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, to examine the feasibility of the areas along National Road 4 and 2. No. 3 and the area next to Kandal province next to Phnom Penh and other places are all rich in workers.
According to the report of the Commission on Vaccination, as of April 5, 2021, Phnom Penh has vaccinated more than 90,000 officials and priority people.
