Indonesian authorities are stepping up rescue efforts and searching for more than 70 people who are reported missing while more than 10,000 are being housed in makeshift camps. Arrested and sent 3 people to court after being angry and disobeying the instructions of the authorities by continuing to drink and have fun without fear of Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): Three people who continued to eat and drink angrily did not listen to the instructions of the competent authorities when Kovid 19 was spreading in the community were arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court This morning, April 6, 2021.
Colonel San Sok Seiha, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, told Fresh News that after several instructions, the message was still not heard, and the police force of the Kork Khleang Sangkat Administration Post of the Sen Sok District Police Inspectorate arrested three people. People while drinking and singing happily on April 4, 2021.
According to Colonel San Sok Seiha, the three men violated health measures in the fight against Kovid 19 in front of a rented room in Boeung Baitong Market, Concrete Road, Trapeang Svay Village, Kork Khleang Commune, Sen Sok District.
The three people are: First name: Aun Ratana, 37 years old, Occupation: mechanic, Wuy Chheng factory, living in a rented room on concrete road, Trapeang Svay village, Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok, Second name: Horun Mony, 30 years old, Occupation: Salesman, living in a room Rent a concrete road in Trapeang Svay village, Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok;
Colonel San Sok Seiha asserted that the strict legal action would continue to be applied to those who were still angry and disobeyed the instructions of the authorities while fighting Kovid 19. He said that in the past, local authorities have advised many times to stop drinking gatherings, but there are still people who do not listen to the instructions, so from now on will take legal action.
