In Kampong Chhnang province, the number of people involved in Som Lo who infected 19 people with Kovid increased to 63, and the authorities called for others who were involved to take immediate tests.
(Kampong Chhnang): At least 63 people were directly and indirectly involved with Som Lo, who was declared infected with Kovid 19 on April 4, 2021. This is according to Dr. Kong Chanthea, Director of the Office of Disease Prevention and Management of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department, confirmed to Fresh News this morning, April 6, 2021.
According to the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department, the 63 people were involved with a tricycle rider and Dr. Pol Bou, the owner of a general medical clinic, both of whom had direct contact with Som Lo. As of April 5, 2021, all 63 stakeholders have taken all samples for testing, but have not yet received the results.
The working group of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department confirmed that this number has not been determined yet, so the working group appealed to the people who were directly and indirectly affected in the above event to meet. Doctors at local health centers to consult and take samples for testing in a timely manner or to be isolated according to health rules.
