In a letter from the Ministry of Health issued by Ms. Ou Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health stated that in the past, the Ministry of Health has already issued guidelines on measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease, especially ban Allow private clinics to treat patients with suspected Kovid-19 disease.
The Ministry of Health said that in order to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease on a large scale in the community, the Ministry of Health would like to issue a final reminder to all private health service owners to further strengthen the implementation of measures to prevent Prevent the spread of Kovid-19 virus to the community by strictly following the following guidelines:
1. Do not allow the examination and treatment of patients suspected of having Kovid-19 and test for Kovid-19 and vaccinate against Kovid-19 (unless authorized by the Ministry of Health).
3. If there is any sign in the definition of Kovid-19, the patient or the person presumed to be suspected of Kovid-19, should wear a mask and guide him to a nearby waiting area, keeping a clear distance. At least one and a half meters (1.5 meters) apart and provide information to the Capital-Provincial Health Department to facilitate the transfer of him to the Chattalysak Center for Kovid-19 patients.
5: Must be vaccinated for 14 days and take samples to check and monitor the health of doctors and staff who have been in contact with patients suspected of having copied-19 disease.
6: There should be a yellow container with a black danger label for storing infectious waste and materials for patients suspected of having Kovid-19 disease, such as masks, wipes and so on. The waste is then collected and burned in a furnace with a temperature above 800 degrees Celsius.
7. All private medical service providers must help educate and disseminate measures to transmit Kovid-19 to staff, patients and their families, as well as to cooperate in preventing the spread of Kovid-19 by washing. Hands with water and soap or alcohol frequently and wear a mask, and maintain a safe distance of at least 1.5 meters or more by applying the three protection measures 3, 3 and 2 involved.
