(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has issued a new guideline asking the Ministry of Health and stakeholders to consider and prepare in advance the possibility of providing home treatment for 19 patients with mild to moderate conditions.
"We now need to predict the sustainability of our hospital," he said. If the disease does not decrease, our hospital will be overflowing with patients, both light and heavy. "So we have to make an arrangement based on the approach of countries with a large number of patients, including the United States, France, Europe and some countries where there are more patients than there can be."
Samdech Techo also emphasized that for home therapists, there must be a mild medical condition and a suitable home that can be treated. On the other hand, if the patient's house is small and can spread to the family, take him to the hospital.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen estimates that at least 50 percent of patients have a mild condition and want to be treated at home.
In addition to considering the possibility of Kovid 19 patients receiving home treatment, Samdech Techo also advised to consider the management of patients from medical visits, as well as financial support and other food.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's initiative to consider home treatment comes after the 19 communicable disease outbreak in the February 20 community event continued to escalate. As of April 5, 2021, yesterday, Cambodia had a total of 2,752 Kovid 19 patients, of which 2,222 were in the February 20 community case. 1,747 people were healed and 979 people were being treated. Twenty-one people died and five died of other illnesses while treating Kovid 19.
