Kampong Cham Provincial Police Rejects Allegations of Deputy Cheung Prey District Deputy Inspector for Cockfighting
(Kampong Cham): The Information and Quick Reaction Team of Kampong Cham Provincial Police confirmed that pictures and information related to the case of violence occurred at the point of the red gravel road in Chheu Teal village, Pdao Chum commune, Cheung Prey district. Kampong Cham province and even charged police officers to pay $ 500 to end the case of violence at the cockfighting location.
In order to avoid public confusion regarding this case, the Information and Quick Reaction Team of Kampong Cham Provincial Police through Fresh News on April 05, 2021, please clarify as follows:
The incident caused the front of the car to be damaged, the front bumper to be broken, and the motorcycle side to break the hood, the engine and the steering wheel. The motorcyclists tried to escape irresponsibly, while the motorcyclists chased after them and started arguing violently, with the motorcyclists hitting the windshield with sticks, causing the rear and side to shatter The left side of the car.
After that, the vehicle side came to complain at the Royal Gendarmerie Command of Cheung Prey District and continued to send a settlement to the specialized police force of the Cheung Prey District Police Inspectorate. The settlement party agreed to accept $ 500 from the motorcycle party and agreed in writing to end the case without any further conditions.
* Second: Based on the explanation from the people in Chheu Teal village, Pdao Chum commune, Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province, and based on the report of the local authority, that during the year 2020 at the point in the cashew forest in Chheu Teal village, Pdao Chum commune, Srok Prey district. Cheung Prey used to have a group of cockfighting thieves from time to time and was also cracked down on by the authorities, but now there is no activity of cockfighting in that area.
* Third: Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commission, please completely reject and reject the content published on the above social media and consider it as exaggeration, disrespect for the profession of journalists and with the intention of slandering individuals. Lieutenant Colonel Kaing Kimhong, Deputy Police Inspector of Cheung Prey District.
At the same time, Kampong Cham Provincial Police would like to express its deep gratitude to the public, journalists and social media for always cooperating to provide information related to security, order and social security in order to take timely measures to prevent and suppress.
(Battambang): While receiving the first rain in 2021, two people lost their lives due to lightning and damaged two houses due to heavy rain and wind in Phnom Proek district, Battambang province on the evening of April 5. This year 2021.
Phnom Proek district administration said that during the rain, there were strong winds and two lightning strikes, causing deaths at two different locations.
Case 1: Occurred in Pich Chenda village, Pich Chenda commune, Phnom Proek district, the victim was a 52-year-old female named Nget Hoeun. Before the incident, he was watching his children grow cassava when lightning struck and killed him on the spot.
Case 2: There was a case of lightning that caused the death of another girl named Ieng Lina, 12 years old, Keat Ling in Phnom Touch village, Pich Chenda commune, Phnom Proek district. Prior to the incident, the girl was riding a bicycle to her mother, but when she returned home about 100 meters from her house, she was struck by lightning and died.
After the inspection, the authorities handed over the body to the relatives for the traditional ceremony.
