The ceremony was attended by General Y Chhean, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense and Chairman of the Pailin Provincial Government Working Group, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Member of Parliament and Mrs. Ban Srey Mom, Provincial Governor and Director of all departments at the hermitage. Yeay Yat, near the foot of Phnom Yat, next to National Road 57, in Wat Village, Sangkat Pailin, Pailin City, Pailin Province, about 2 km from the provincial town.
According to Ms. Ban Srey Mom, the prayer for happiness and prosperity now is to get the blessing from Mrs. Yat, who has the power to take care of the land of diamonds. Throughout Pailin province and the country to avoid natural disasters and other diseases, especially to avoid the disease Covid-19 (Covid-19) that is spreading in the country and around the world.
On that occasion, although Pailin province has not yet had a case of Kovid-19 exploding into the community, on behalf of the provincial leadership, Ms. Ban Srey Mom called on people throughout the province to remain vigilant to protect themselves from This vicious disease and other infectious diseases by implementing the "3 prevent 3" measures of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, as well as measures of the Ministry of Health.
It should be noted that the large statue of Yeay Yat, located in the hermitage near the foot of Phnom Yat, was built in April 2011 at the direct expense of General Y Chhean and Mrs. Ban Srey Mom, made of sandstone in the province. Kampong Thom has a height of 3.80 meters, a throne size of 2.40 square meters and a total weight of 32 tons.
