(Phnom Penh): On the night of April 5, 2021, the authorities and health officials said that 20 more Orussey Market traders were found positive Kovid 19, bringing the number to 36. With the number of infections so high, the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority would like to continue to call on other traders to immediately take samples at Bak Touk High School, as you have already collected more than 1,000 samples.
7 Makara District Governor Lim Sophea and the report of the Orussey Market Commission said that last night, another 20 traders were found positive Kovid, leading to an increase of 36 people. However, despite warnings and appeals from authorities, more than 1,000 of the more than 7,000 traders have already taken samples.
The Phnom Penh Municipal Administration calls on other traders to immediately take samples and continue to make the correct measurements at home, and local authorities must monitor in their villages or sangkats to see who sells in Orussey Market. Get a sample and make a solid catalyst.
Traders who do not do the right thing will be fined, as stated in the new Kovid 19 law.
According to the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority, allowing traders to inspect the sample is not a coercion related to their rights and freedoms, but related to their primary health problems to determine which traders have Kovid-19 disease and which traders do not. Contains Kovid-19 disease.
The governor of 7 Makara district called on the people, traders and those who saw the name of the Kovid at Orussey Market to immediately take a sample to find 19 Kovid, and if they do not agree and continue to evade, the authorities will take legal action when It was found that these individuals became infected with Kovid due to previous contact with patients.
On the night of April 3, 2021, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration decided to temporarily suspend the entry and exit of O'Russey Market for 14 days. The suspension comes after a total of six vendors, deputy market chiefs and security guards were diagnosed with 19 cases of Kovid.
