The five recommendations include:
* First, the National Committee for the Promotion of One Village, One Product Movement, the Ministry of Commerce and the relevant ministries must continue to cooperate and coordinate smoothly to promote the use of Cambodian products, a broad understanding of the quality of Cambodian products. Each provides producers with skills in the production process, quality improvement, product safety, processing and packaging.
* Second: The National Committee for Promoting the Movement of One Village, One Product, the Committee for Promoting the Movement of One Village, One Product, the Capital-Province, the Ministry of Commerce and relevant ministries and institutions must cooperate with the private sector to organize online marketing through technology to help Khmer products to sell and launch. In the event of various product exhibitions both in the country and abroad and at Cambodian representative offices abroad.
* Third: The National Committee for the Promotion of One Village, One Product Movement and the Ministry of Commerce must jointly develop a roadmap for a One Village, One Product product in order to ensure the sustainability of the uniqueness produced by the people in one or more villages as a product. Reflects traditional cultural characteristics, both traditional and contemporary.
