Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Delegate of the Royal Government in charge of the General Department of Taxation, expressed his gratitude to the taxpayers and tax service providers who were happy and supported the tax services introduced in the system. This online.
The Minister said that the factors that prepare to use this information technology system is to strengthen good governance and transparency leading to good governance. Therefore, the sustainability of revenue as well as continued revenue growth is due to the strengthening of good governance.
He said that in the difficult circumstances of the economic crisis caused by the impact of Covid-19, if the information technology system is not organized in a proactive and timely manner, the revenue may be difficult to manage and collect tax revenue.
"I will continue to work hard to develop more IT programs to improve tax services," he said.
He said that the community event on February 20, the General Department of Taxation has adhered to the Royal Government's policy to prevent 19 cases of Kovid, by reducing the attendance of officials by 90 percent and have organized the rotation of officials and assigned to work. Home day and night to ensure the sustainability of the management of tax revenue collection to the state and the provision of services to taxpayers.
Minister Ith Sam Heng Calls on Civil Servants of the Ministry of Labor to Volunteer Kovid-19 Vaccine
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, on April 05, 2021, inspected the Kovid-19 vaccination campaign for civil servants under the auspices of the Ministry of Labor. Officials of the Ministry of Labor, as well as workers, participate in the Kovid-19 vaccination on a voluntary basis.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that the Kovid-19 vaccine is a new tool in addition to the existing health measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and save lives, which helps individuals avoid serious illness when infected with Kovid-19 and Reduce hospitalization.
The Kovid-19 vaccine currently being used in Cambodia is a vaccine that has been thoroughly tested for safety and efficacy and is being used in countries in the region and around the world, some of which have already been vaccinated by tens of millions.
Voluntary vaccinations to protect yourself, your family and your community from the Kovid-19 virus can invade your home and your community, endangering public health, he said. As well as having a serious impact on the family economy as well as our national economy.
At the same time, even if individuals have already been vaccinated, it must be remembered that they must continue to participate in monitoring and preventing the risk of transmission of Kovid-19 to reduce the economic and social impact by continuing to implement three measures: 3. Protect against the transmission of Kovid-19 virus in communities in Cambodia, as directed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Please be informed that the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo, has assigned the Kovid-19 Vaccination Commission in collaboration with ministries and institutions of local authorities at all levels to launch a large-scale vaccination campaign throughout the country.
In this campaign, the Ministry of Health team is preparing to vaccinate more than 740,000 priority groups for the first dose of Sinovak vaccine starting April 1, 2021. On the morning of April 3, 2021, civil servants of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training were ready to receive the Kovid-19 vaccine, which was held at the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. Once.
The vaccination campaign is organized by the Kovid-19 Vaccination Commission in a nationwide framework in collaboration with the Kovid-19 Vaccination Sub-Committee of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training for the purpose of preventing and preventing the spread of the disease. Kovid-19 disease.
