General Neth Savoeun Chairs a Meeting on Measures to Stabilize Security, Public Order and Social Security on the Occasion of Khmer New Year
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of April 5, 2021, General Santebandit Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, chaired a meeting on "Measures to ensure stability, security, public order and social security on the occasion of Khmer New Year". Attended by all Deputy Commissioners, Heads of Departments, Relevant Units and Capital-Provincial Police Commissioners.
After reading the detailed contents of the instruction on measures to ensure stability, security, public order and social safety during the traditional Khmer New Year by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, then Gen. Santi Dr. Neth Savoeun, Police Commissioner The nation has set out the following general principles:
* First, all departments, subordinate units and the Capital-Provincial Police Commission must announce the high point to strengthen security measures and public order for the traditional Khmer New Year, especially in the priority destinations, pagodas, resorts and entertainment venues, with a plan to implement. Clear.
* Second: All departments and units must have the following practical work program:
A: Shift 24/7 to ensure job sustainability
B: To strengthen the command team in the departments, units and the Capital-Provincial Police Commission to receive the request of the public and to be ready, means, means, equipment and materials to intervene to solve the people in a timely manner.
