Those who enter Kampong Chhnang province from today onwards will be required to do 14 days of testing and will be required to take a sample for testing.
(Kampong Chhnang): The administration of Kampong Chhnang province has confirmed that from April 5, 2021, those who enter Kampong Chhnang province will be required to undergo 14 days of testing and will be required to take samples for testing. This is according to the instructions on strengthening some measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 during the New Year and strengthen security, safety, public order and hygiene to celebrate the traditional New Year, which was received by Fresh News.
The provincial administration has instructed the commune / sangkat authorities and the commune / sangkat administrative police station to make a clear list of people in their jurisdiction. How many permanent members does each family have? How many members go to work far away? Where? In particular, research into those who go to work in high-risk areas with Kovid 19.
Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration added that the grip and control of every family member to:
* Advise them not to return home, should visit each other online * If they arrive immediately, be controlled and put on a 14-day biopsy and report to a doctor to get a sample for testing. The local authority is responsible for implementing administrative measures in accordance with the laws and regulations in force.
