For more details, please read the instructions below: More than 1.6 tons of ammunition extracted from an old ship in Kampong Cham was burned
The burning ceremony of 1.6 tons of unexploded ordnance was presided over by Lt. Gen. Phal Samon, Deputy Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center, with the participation of a number of working groups. The cremation site is located in Veal village, Meanchey commune, Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province.
According to Colonel Eam Vann's report, according to the plan, the team will neutralize 90% of the well-formed and safe ammunition for museum display and destroy 10% of the deformed ammunition. Fragile can not be neutralized.
It should be noted that the Marine ship that sank during the civil war in Cambodia in the 1972s sank in the river bottom to a depth of 27.5 meters and covered with a lot of sand on top. At this point, the task force finds it difficult to collect ammunition scattered around the warship.
The operation to clear unexploded ordnance buried under the water at this point is an unprecedented historical achievement for Cambodia. No land, so it is another pride for the Cambodian nation.
