(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration on April 05, 2021 issued guidelines on tightening the implementation of security measures, safety, order and order and measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 during the holidays. Khmer New Year, a traditional Khmer festival in Phnom Penh. This is according to the instructions received by Fresh News.
The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has instructed the people, youths, workers and the general public to participate in the implementation of security measures, safety, order and order and measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 as follows:
* First, to increase the vigilance of candles, incense, stoves, the use of fuel, gas and electricity to prevent future fires and to avoid loss of property and lives of ordinary people.
* Second, it is strictly forbidden to gamble of any kind and to spray water, water cannons, powder, charcoal, whips or other devices, firecrackers and other explosives, which are illegal and seriously harmful. To the beautiful traditions of the society
* Third: Avoid unnecessary travel or accommodation and avoid traveling or traveling to other provinces, which may be at high risk of transmitting Kovid-19 to other individuals, families and In the community, it is worse because Phnom Penh has been designated by the Ministry of Health as one of the five geographical locations of the capital-province with the outbreak of Kovid-19 in the "Community Event 20 February 2021"
