BEIJING (Reuters) - A report submitted to the US House of Representatives recently claimed that Hong Kong was no longer autonomous, and therefore no longer favored by the United States.
Clearly, the new US administration has continued its policy attitude toward Hong Kong under the Trump administration. This act angrily interfered in China's internal affairs, and the Chinese side expressed strong dissatisfaction and strong opposition to this.
In general, some people on the US side are still trying to prevent China's development by using Hong Kong as a shield. But such attempts will be in vain and will fail. In the middle of last year, the US side announced that it would no longer provide special concessions to Hong Kong, but ultimately did not gain any influence. Hong Kong continued to prosper.
