(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, and Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, on Sunday, April 4, 2021, inspected the Kovid 19 vaccination process of Sinovak to civil servants of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. Shipping.
The Ministry of Public Works, as well as other ministries and institutions, launched the Sinovak vaccination campaign for government officials on April 1. According to the plan, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport will provide about 1,993 officials. In the past three days, the Ministry has injected about 1,219 people.
On that occasion, both the Senior Minister and Mr. Hun Many emphasized the importance of the Kovid 19 vaccine in the fight against Kovid 19 disease that is spreading in Cambodia as well as the world.
Mr. Sun Chanthol highlighted that Kovid 19 vaccine is a new tool in addition to the existing health measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and save lives by helping individuals to avoid serious illness when infected with Kovid 19 and reduce the risk. Hospitalized.
In particular, Mr. Hun Many said that the vaccine is a necessary solution to protect people and communities as a whole from any large-scale outbreak.
Both Senior Minister Sun Chanthol and Mr. Hun Many expressed their thoughts and efforts of the Royal Government in seeking vaccines for the people. The Royal Government plans to provide vaccines to at least 10 million people.
Mr. Sun Chanthol said, "The Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo, has been very thoughtful in protecting the lives of the people from the 199 outbreak of Kovid and has worked hard to find vaccines for our people." "This is an example, a great value of our leaders."
Separately, Mr. HUN Many confirmed that the Royal Government has made efforts to mobilize to find vaccines from all directions through flexible mechanisms for people across the country to receive vaccines.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol and Mr. Hun Many called on civil servants as well as those who have registered or given priority to vaccination to hurry up to get vaccinated to protect their health and prevent the spread of disease in Community.
Mr. Sun Chanthol and Mr. Hun Many also reminded the vaccinators that even after vaccination, do not forget to follow the rules recommended by the Ministry of Health. In particular, the "3 do not protect" because even after vaccination, the virus is still contagious. It just does not cause serious health problems and heals faster than you do not get vaccinated.
It should be noted that during the inspection visit to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Sun Chanthol invited Mr. Hun Many to inspect the achievements of the Ministry of Public Service Providers and Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport.
