Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department confirmed that the 19 infected Kovid was a 36-year-old Cambodian man named Som Lo, who worked at a factory in Phnom Penh, and received the second "positive" test result on April 4. This year 2021.
Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department revealed the travel history of the above man before announcing the birth of Kovid 19 as follows:
He came to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hospital on Monday, March 29, 2021 for a check-up with a fever over 38 degrees Celsius with symptoms of shortness of breath and nausea. Doctors referred the man to a special care team to test for Kovid-19.
After the test, the man was instructed and allowed to return home to have a catheterization and wait for the test results. The next day, at 11:00 AM, the man was admitted to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hospital and was treated separately at the Infectious Diseases Unit of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hospital.
According to the interrogation, the man started coughing and had difficulty breathing on March 28, 2021. The next morning, on the 29th of the same month, at 4:00 AM, he rode a motorbike to Kampong Chhnang province at his home in Mong Barang village, Sangkat P'er, Kampong Chhnang city, Kampong Chhnang province at 6:30 am. . At 8:00, he traveled to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hospital with his wife on a motorbike.
