Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Temporarily Suspends Access to Part of Rolok Dam Area After Finding Kovid
According to a letter from the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration, received by Fresh News today, the administration would like to inform the residents of the Rolok Dam area: Taken from the people in the Rolok Dam area since March 27, 2021, it is confirmed that there are 19 positive cases of Kovid virus related to people in that area.
In order to prevent the spread of Kovid-19, the provincial administration decided to close the area immediately from the Rolok Dam Police Headquarters to Rumduol Cheung Phnom (Group 6) and from the railway (both roads) in the back. Sakura School, Cambodia-Japan Friendship to the seashore, no further entry and exit of the area.
The team to search for and detect suspected cases of Kovid-19 will conduct interviews with stakeholders at the site, and the provincial health department's emergency response team will collect samples from all residents in the area to test for Kovid virus. 5-19.
In this regard, the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration has decided to temporarily suspend all kinds of businesses and sales of the local people and set up a Chatalisak Center for 14 days from the time of this notification until further notice. All citizens must take a test sample and perform a catheterization in accordance with the instructions of the Ministry of Health.
