(Phnom Penh): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Commission for Kovid Vaccination 19 (KV 19), on April 4, 2021, announced that it strictly forbids some ministries and institutions to stop providing Kovid 19 vaccine. To an unnamed outsider on the priority list immediately.
Ms. Ou Vandin's announcement came after it was observed that some ministries had vaccinated 19 non-civil servants within the framework of their ministries. In a voicemail obtained by Fresh News, Ms. O Vandin said that the fact that the Ministry brought outsiders to be vaccinated in the ministry thus led to a shortage of vaccines according to the distribution of vaccines that had already been prepared.
"If each ministry keeps injecting other people who are not their own officials, it will reduce the number of vaccines that we plan to provide to civil servants under each ministry," she said. . So from tomorrow, I would like to place an order, because this is a big thing, not a small thing.
Ms. O Vandin called on the chair of the Kovid 19 Vaccination Sub-Committee in the ministries and institutions not to add other staff and from tomorrow she asked the vaccination team to conduct the most thorough inspection and verification of the existing list. . She warned the vaccination team that if the vaccinators were not on the list, vaccinations would not be allowed.
