Svay Rieng Provincial Administration calls on all people to be very careful, especially to adhere to the measures of the head of the Royal Government "3 protect 3 do not" and if there is no need to stay in the house to cut the roots together Of Kovid-19, starting from the cooperation of each and every citizen.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. An Sothyta, an expert in the condominium sector, claims that the condominium sector is still a good sector, a new type of housing to provide Cambodians with modern living.
Such claims by Ms. An Sothyta argued that due to the price in the condominium sector is affordable compared to real estate projects. On the other hand, living in a condominium is easy and safe.
Ms. An Sothyta stated, "I think the condominium sector is still a good sector as a new type of housing for the people of Cambodia, although this sector is new for 5 years."
Ms. An Sothyta continued, "Because the price is reasonable compared to real estate projects and makes the lives of Cambodians easier and safer, especially easy to maintain."
In addition, Ms. An Sothyta emphasized that in this context and new trends, the condominium sector is still at the forefront, especially condominiums located in the center of Phnom Penh.
On the issue of Kovid-19, Ms. An Sothyta felt that there must be a solution to get rid of this impact, and she also proposed to unite to protect to avoid the problems we are facing.
Ms. An Sothyta said that comparing Cambodia with other developed countries in Asia in relation to the Kovid-19 issue, Cambodia still ranks best in terms of housing in the condominium sector.
According to her, up to now, there are between 100 and 150 condominiums in Phnom Penh.
She said that if you look at the situation on the condominium sector in Cambodia, compared to the end of 2020 and the beginning of 2021, the decline in the condominium sector is between 50-60% of the total sales. . The decline was due to Kovid 19.
She said the condominium sector was classified as the residential sector of the real estate sector, so the housing sector was less affected by Kovid 19 compared to other sectors.
