On Saturday, 10 of the rebels met on video to discuss the unrest in Myanmar and condemned the Myanmar military's use of live ammunition against protesters and said they were standing. With the people of Myanmar demanding an end to the military regime.
The 10 rebels are signatories to a major ceasefire agreement reached by Aung San Suu Kyi's government. But now they have suggested that the deal could be reviewed.
This publication is in stark contrast to the fact that Gen. Neth Savoeun, now in good health, has been leading the national police force across the country in operations to maintain security, public order and social safety, especially in the fight against the Kovid War. 19 as well as on the occasion of the upcoming Khmer New Year.
The spokesperson of the General Commission of the National Police would like to declare and completely reject the fabricated information that not only insults the honor of the life of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, the Senior Commander of the National Police Force, but also intends to cause Chaos in the ranks of the National Police will undermine stability, security and social order.
A spokesman for the National Police General Commission stressed that "We strongly condemn the unscrupulous acts of these unscrupulous persons and request that the specialized unit investigate and find the perpetrators, including factions and masterminds, and bring them to justice." The law is in force. ”
At the same time, the spokesperson of the General Commission of the National Police called on the public, journalists, especially social media, not to be confused and asked not to share this false information to avoid making it difficult to carry out the research tasks of the specialized department and may face Implementing the professional principles of law enforcement officers.
