Authorities begin excavating Peanut Lake to save animal and fish life
Excavation took place on the afternoon of April 3, 2021, after the Siem Reap provincial administration agreed to the community's request as the lake dried up during the dry season this year.
The Siem Reap Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has started sending machinery to Pea Reang Lake and has gradually started digging to restore the lake. According to the plan, the excavation phase is for the first rescue of thousands of species that may be lost in the near future as the water dries up this dry season.
The President of Boeung Pearang Ecotourism Community applauded this work and thanked the provincial leaders for saving the biodiversity in this conservation lake for the benefit of the whole community. According to Kong Mongkul, in a proposal approved by the Ministry of Agriculture, it is understood that the lake will be excavated to cover more than 2,000 hectares and a depth of 4 meters. However, at this stage, not all have been excavated, waiting for a suitable time.
It should be noted that Pearang Lake is located in the southern part of Siem Reap city and is adjacent to Sangkat Chreav and Sangkat Chong Kneas, Siem Reap city. This lake is a natural tourist resort near Siem Reap and is always full of tourists to visit, especially bird watching. Honorary Dr. Men Sam An Donates US $ 2,000 on the Occasion of the 158th Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2021
