A power line caught fire in a house in Srey Snom district, completely damaged
(Siem Reap Province): A house in Srey Snom district was completely burnt down while the owner went out. The house fire occurred on April 3, 2021 at 12:15 pm in Maung Khang Tbong village, Maung commune, Srey Snom district, Siem Reap province.
Colonel Dut Khon, deputy commissioner in charge of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Office, said that the owner of the house that caught fire was Sar Sol, a 41-year-old male farmer. The house measures 9 meters x 6 meters, built of stone under wood, on a galvanized roof, about 50 percent flammable. Four beds, four closets and a television were also set on fire.
