Opinion: Samdech Techo Hun Sen Vireak Kolbot, who is loyal to the King and the throne
(Phnom Penh): April 4 has been set as the official birthday of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia. As of April 4, 2021, it has been 51 years since the date of this year was chosen as the date of birth.
In fact, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was born at 12 o'clock on Tuesday, August 15, 1952. So why use April 4th as your official birthday?
April 4 is the day that Samdech Techo Prime Minister decided to enter Prey Maki at the call of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk to liberate the throne and regain the monarchy after the regime was overthrown by Lon Nol's faction. With the support of the US Empire, it was looted and taken on March 18, 1970.
Techo Sen, a Khmer born in rural areas along the Mekong River and raised during the monarchy under Samdech Norodom Sihanouk, originally intended to be just an ordinary teacher while society was There was peace and progress towards development at that time.
But the effects of the expansion of US power in Asia and the hunger for power of General Lon Nol and Prince Sisowath Sirimatak undermined national peace and led to an illegal coup d'état on the 18th. March 1970: Seizes the Sangkum Reastr Niyum regime and overthrows the monarchy in Cambodia.
The coup d'état, backed by US budget ideas and poisonous tactics, plunged Cambodian society into disrepair. Samdech Techo and loyalist Samdech Norodom Sihanouk, loyalists of the monarchy, were willing to give up the happiness of their youth into the jungle to fight for power and return the throne from the US-backed illegal regime.
On the battlefield for the monarchy, for the royal family, for the father of the Khmer independence, Samdech Techo was wounded on the battlefield and left blind in the left eye due to artillery shells on the battlefield in Kampong Cham province on April 16, 1975. The day before, the resistance movement had completely taken over Phnom Penh from Lon Nol. This is a tragic legacy for Techo Sen and left to this day.
Losing one eye on the battlefield to liberate the monarchy and hand over the throne to Samdech Norodom Sihanouk is already a painful and tragic story. But what made this fighter even more painful and tragic was that his struggle did not go as he wished, because the victory was betrayed by Pol Pot and continued to be robbed without handing over power to Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and the throne. And the monarchy is still buried.
Despite the failure and failure to recapture the regime and the throne back to Samdech Norodom Sihanouk. But the heartfelt devotion to the throne to Samdech Norodom Sihanouk has not been lost for Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Through the struggle and hardships of nearly 20 years of national political events, Samdech Techo Hun Sen finally achieved his goal of bringing back the monarchy and the throne to the father of Khmer independence, Norodom Sihanouk, in 1993 will bring harmony in Cambodian society as well.
In the power of the Royal Government since 1993, after the re-establishment of the monarchy, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has always declared his determination to prevent this regime from being overthrown.
In addition to demonstrating his commitment to protecting the throne and the royal family, Samdech Techo, as a leader, has spoken out against the insults of the king and royal family by some politicians and immoral people who are hiding abroad.
Samdech Techo's Husband to the Throne and the Monarchy Leads to the Admiration of His Majesty the King Father of Khmer Independence, Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia, Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, as well as the King of Cambodia, His Majesty the King His Majesty Norodom Sihamoni. This loyalty of Samdech Techo was also chosen by Samdech Norodom Sihanouk as a Dharma child.
Apart from his loyalty and devotion to the throne, Samdech Techo Hun Sen is also a Khmer son who is loyal to the nation and the people. This loyalty and loyalty motivated the head of the Royal Government to work tirelessly to build national development and improve the lives of the people to be better and more prosperous. Escape from a nation with a low status and honor, full of superiority today.
The heroic example of Samdech Techo's leadership has been greatly appreciated by His Majesty the King, His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia and the King of Cambodia.
He continued, "The Royal Government, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, the people of our nation, all of us, work tirelessly to build the nation for Cambodia, we will absolutely leave the weak to the maximum to hold on to the status of power." One in the world. This is very good, unity, but one way, the Royal Government has HE Hun Sen as the head of the National Assembly, all our people are united.
In his congratulatory message to Samdech Techo on the birthday of the Khmer Queen Mother Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the King emphasized that "Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo is the smartest and most talented leader in building national achievements in all areas. "We have achieved great success for the benefit of the nation, the motherland and the people of Cambodia, as well as strived to eradicate poverty in society and enhance the prestige of our nation on the international stage."
He continued, "The people of Cambodia, like me, are very satisfied with the continuous progress day and night under the talented leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia."
On the occasion of the day of Samdech Techo's resignation to seize the monarchy and the throne, the King and Queen have blessed Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, as well as their sons and daughters and grandsons. Granddaughter has achieved new successes in the noble mission for the benefit of the nation and the people of Cambodia, and may the Buddha bless you with age, class, happiness and strength.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's loyalty and loyalty to the King to the throne has led Cambodian society to experience happiness, unity and prosperity for more than 20 years. May the heroic example of Samdech Techo Sen's loyalty to the nation, to the king, to the throne, to the people continue to permeate the Khmer people of all generations for the sake of harmony in Cambodian society.
