(Kandal): 212 Kovid-19 patients who were treated at Kovid-19 Medical Center, Koh Thom District, Kandal Province were recovered by the authorities and allowed to return to their respective homes, but had to be treated separately. 14 more days. Only 23 are still receiving treatment.
According to the source, the 212 patients were tested twice for the virus, which was negative, so the authorities allowed them to go home for another 14 days, and on the 13th day, they were asked to do so. He must come to give the final sample again to confirm more details.
It should be reminded that Kovid-19 Medical Center, Koh Thom District, was announced by the Kandal Provincial Administration on March 12, 2021, with Yongyuan Casino located in Chrey Thom Village, Sampov Poun Commune, Koh Thom District as a temporary treatment center. On April 2, 2021, 235 Kovid-19 patients were treated.
