10-year-old boy killed and thrown into the forest in Sangkat Kbal Koh, Khan Chbar Ampov
(Phnom Penh): A 10-year-old boy missing from his home was found dead in the forest on April 2, 2021, along Tiger Road in Boang Kanh 1 Village, Prek Eang Sangkat, Chbar Ampov District. Suspected murder case. The victim was identified as Chea Bunheng, a resident of Chroy Ampil village, Kbal Koh commune.
On March 31, 2021, at 7 pm, the parents of the 10-year-old boy reported to the Chbar Ampov district police after the boy did not return home after playing football. Witnesses confirmed to the family that they saw the child victim riding a motorbike before disappearing.
The Child Protection Unit received the information on April 1, 2021 and provided assistance to the police to find the child victims, and the joint team checked the security cameras on the streets until 8 pm on the 1st. April The child victim is still missing and the investigation is continuing.
At 4:30 pm on April 2, 2021, the body of a child was found in a bush near a main road in Sangkat Preng Eang, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh. The Homicide Investigation Team (HIT) and the Technical and Scientific (FST) Team of the Child Protection Unit (CPU) inspected the scene and liaised with police officers from the Criminal Police Department and the Technical and Scientific Department to investigate.
After that, the police of the Technical and Scientific Office, CPU and Duke Dr. Nong Sovannaroth, Phnom Penh forensic doctor, inspected the scene and found a pair of skin (of the victim boy) and the body of the victim boy. Face and lower teeth on both sides (two sides). The body is now being handed over to the family for a traditional ceremony, while authorities are searching to arrest the killer and bring him to justice.
