In the last month, the number of loan refinancing applications has increased significantly after the outbreak of the "February 20" community event
(Phnom Penh): Kaing Tong Ngy, spokesman for the Cambodian Microfinance Association, said that in the past four weeks, many customers have applied for credit restructuring after the third outbreak of the 19 19th Kovid. Or the February 20 community event.
"We anticipate that lending requests will jump even further in the future," he said. "Such estimates suggest that in 2020, about 20,000 customers applied for credit restructuring in just one week."
He added that the outbreak of the February 20 event will further increase the number of loan applications, but not up to 20,000 requests per week as in 2020.
Please be informed that the Ministry of Economy and Finance has recently launched a $ 200 million credit guarantee scheme to rehabilitate the business of the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation. The Business Recovery Credit Guarantee Program aims to support micro, small and medium enterprises, and large businesses in expanding access to financing from participating financial institutions (PFIs) for working capital, investment, and expansion. Business.
Mr. Kaing Tong Ngy also stated that the approximately $ 200 million invested by the Royal Government on credit guarantee projects to rehabilitate businesses has encouraged MFIs to provide more loans to small and medium enterprises in Cambodia. This small and medium business is necessary to drive the momentum and growth of the economy, small and medium enterprises have played an important role in driving the local economy.
