According to the Cambodian Rice Federation, the largest export market for the quarter was to China and Hong Kong and Macau Autonomous Region, with 85,370 tonnes, or 55.55 tonnes. %.
However, the trend of rice exports in March 2021 has been gradually recovering, increasing by 84.66% compared to February, up from 41,949 tons in the month. February to 77,466 tons in March, while February compared to January increased by only 22%.
The first quarter of 2021 was the year with the lowest exports than the quarters of the last five years. The main reason for the delay in the delivery of goods to overseas buyers, especially to the target countries in the European Union is the lack of containers for rice and shipping costs. The sea continues to be more expensive compared to the same period of the last five years, with gaps more than five times higher.
Most of the rice exports in the first quarter of 2021 were luxury fragrant rice and plain fragrant rice, accounting for more than half of total exports.
