MANILA, March 2 (Xinhua) - The Philippines has recorded 15,310 new cases of Kovid-19 in the last 24 hours, the health authorities said on Friday. This is according to a release by the Xinhua news agency.
It is the highest daily infection figure ever since the Southeast Asian country was hit by the global pandemic in January 2020.
Combined with the new cases, the total number of cases across the Philippines has risen to 771,497, including 13,320, after 17 new cases were found today.
The Philippines, with a total population of 110 million, has so far tested 9.5 million people.
