Minister of Commerce: Kovid 19 is an opportunity for Cambodia to reform to strengthen trade development and economic resilience
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, emphasized that Cambodia has turned the Kovid-19 crisis into an opportunity for reform in the country, and the Ministry of Commerce has worked hard to implement the Royal Government's political program and strategy to boost domestic production. To supply market demand and diversify the export sector to promote regional and global economic and trade integration.
The Minister emphasized this on the occasion of presiding over the opening of the Conference on Business Review 2020 and the direction of business implementation 2021 at the Ministry on Thursday morning, April 1, 2021 with the participation and live video conference. From more than 200 leaders and civil servants of the Ministry and the Department of Commerce at all levels.
On that occasion, Mr. Pan Sosak informed the meeting about the achievements in 2020 and the maintenance of export growth of 16.7%, similar to 2019, efforts to diversify the market and attract new investment through negotiations to establish trade zones. Bilateral and multilateral liberalization, strengthening the field of intellectual property and consumer protection, and the introduction of modern information technology systems to improve public services and facilitate business.
