(Phnom Penh): The launch of relations and cooperation between Cambodia and China has made the Chinese government provide a lot of support to the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against Kovid 19.
In addition to providing expert assistance and medical equipment for the fight against Kovid 19, the Chinese government has provided about 1.3 million doses of Kovid 19 Sinofam vaccine to the Royal Government of Cambodia for injection. The Chinese ambassador to Cambodia, Wang Winthean, confirmed that Cambodia was the first country in which the Chinese government had provided 19 Kovid vaccines.
In addition to providing assistance, the Chinese government has facilitated the purchase of 1.5 million doses of Sinovak vaccine in a short period of time and at a special price. These gestures show the strong will of the government and the people to participate in the fight against Kovid 19 in Cambodia.
In this interview, the Chinese ambassador asserted that as long as 19 cases of Kovid 19 in Cambodia are not over, Chinese government assistance to Cambodia to fight Kovid 19 will not end.
The following is an excerpt from an interview between Chinese Ambassador Wang Vinthean and Cambodian journalists on vaccination assistance and cooperation against 19 cases of measles in Cambodia:
Q: Ambassador, this is my first question. What do you think about the measures taken to prevent Kovid 19 and the acceleration of vaccination of citizens of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the past and now?
A: As a diplomat, I should not actually comment on Cambodia's internal affairs, but he raised a question and I would like to express my personal feelings:
At first, I thought that under the wise leadership of Prime Minister Hun Sen, the prevention of viral diseases in Cambodia was well implemented. And Cambodia is one of the countries with the best results in the fight against the virus, also recognized by the international community.
The second is to adhere to the principle of "taking the people as a whole." To alleviate the burden of the people, the government has put in place policies to provide free medical care and vaccinations to the population, provide subsidies to families affected by the Kovid virus and strive to Rescue people infected with Kovid-19 virus.
Third, Cambodia pays attention to international cooperation on the prevention of Kovid-19 virus. Cambodia attaches great importance to cooperation with the WHO office in Cambodia, as well as China and friendly countries. With the outbreak of the virus, Cambodia has also provided aid in the form of anti-virus materials to friendly countries such as China.
A: China and Cambodia are steel friends and a common destiny community that always supports and helps each other. Since the outbreak of Kovid-19 virus, the people of the two countries have come together to help each other, setting an example of international cooperation in the fight against the virus.
While China is in the most difficult period of prevention of Kovid-19 virus, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia in Freedom and Dignity And the happiness that both of them wished to bestow upon the Chinese people in the form of material gifts and sublime royal wealth.
Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, pays an urgent visit to China while it is snowing heavily. The first anti-virus material that Wuhan received from abroad was from Cambodia.
Q: At this point, I would like to open a circle of nails to ask His Excellency about Samdech Techo's visit to China on February 5, 2020, while some countries discriminated against China at that time because of Kovid 19. Is it because Hun Sen's visit to China at that time excited the Chinese government and people that it is one of the main reasons why China is helping Cambodia now?
The actual visit of this visit shows the support of the Prime Minister and the Cambodian people to the Chinese side in the fight against the virus, confirming the core meaning of the common destiny community between China and Cambodia, as a proverb says. Know good friends in difficult times. Also inscribed in the history of Sino-Cambodian relations.
* Question: The vaccine that China provides to Cambodia has been well received by the Cambodian people in general, but this Chinese vaccine has also become the subject of some political profiteers, taking the Chinese vaccine as a topic of attack and fear that the Chinese vaccine makes Dangerous to death and blamed the Cambodian government for using Chinese vaccine to kill its own people. What is your explanation for this?
A: The safety and efficacy of Chinese vaccines are well documented. At present, more than 70 countries have allowed the use of Chinese vaccines. According to figures, the number of vaccines injected in China is more than 120 million doses. In Cambodia, tens of thousands of Chinese vaccinators have not seen any serious reactions.
Some people have been spreading rumors on the Internet that Chinese vaccines are not safe. Some people are doing this in order to attract the attention of others. In Cambodia.
There is a Chinese proverb that says, "The truth of the matter can overcome all rumors." The safety and efficacy of Chinese vaccines will be confirmed to you later. Concerning the rumors that the Cambodian government is using Chinese vaccines to kill its own people, this is a nonsense.
Online rumors can have some negative effects. Because Kovid-19 virus is a new problem and the vaccine is a new thing. All of you may have to wait a while longer. Ideally, the government should continue to strengthen vaccination awareness campaigns to make people more aware of vaccines as an effective tool to stop the spread of this serious Kovid-19 virus.
Therefore, whether it is a Chinese vaccine or another vaccine that can help the Cambodian people to cope with the harassment of Kovid-19 virus can play an active role in the fight against the virus, any kind of vaccine. The whole technical problem should not be used as a political treadmill.
Last night, the Minister of Health and I attended the handover ceremony, and I also mentioned that the Chinese side will not only continue to provide grants in the form of vaccines, but also continue to prioritize the purchase of vaccines for the Cambodian side.
A: I would like to inform my Cambodian friends that China and Cambodia are good brothers and sisters who are like hands and feet, good friends who always help each other. As long as Kovid disease in Cambodia is not over, Chinese aid to Cambodia cannot be stopped. In the fight against smallpox, the Chinese people continue to support the Cambodian people.
Currently, the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, in compliance with the requirements of the Ministry of Health of Cambodia and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, has decided to provide voluntary vaccinations to Chinese citizens living in Cambodia, including Hong Kong and Macau nationals. And Taiwan, the list has already been handed over to the Cambodian side.
Finally, I wish all my friends good health and success in all their endeavors. Thank you!
