Mr. Sam Soeun reduced the room rate by 50% for one month
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sam Soeun, an adviser to the Royal Government and his wife, Phal Vanna, achieved a 50% reduction in room rates throughout April for workers and employees who are renting their rooms.
In addition to reducing the room rate for one month, Mr. Sam Soeun also reduced the price of electricity to 600 riel per kilowatt hour for nine months and did not charge for water until the end of 2021. Mr. Sam Soeun confirmed that he had 160 rooms for rent to workers.
Mr. Sam Soeun confirmed that he decided not to charge one month's room rent, as well as to reduce the price of electricity and water throughout the year 2021 to share the hardships of workers who are suffering from the Kovid 19 crisis. In particular, respect the recommendations and appeals of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who paid attention to the difficulties of workers.
Please note that Samdech Techo Hun Sen appealed to landlords and landlords across the country to reduce wages or not charge to alleviate the hardships of workers and employees.
Through this appeal, many landlords and tenants have already announced that they do not charge or reduce their rents and rooms. Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers these gestures as a model in society and a culture of sharing difficulties in society.
