This is confirmed in the message of Samdech Techo Prime Minister after Samdech has already approved the Master Plan for Tourism Development in Siem Reap 2021-2035 on March 31, 2021.
In the message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in addition to the famous Angkor Wat and many other ancient temples that cover an area of 401 square kilometers, Siem Reap also has many other rich resources, especially tourist areas. The six priorities include "Preah Jayavarman-Norodom National Park", "Phnom Kulen", the area around the Banteay Srei Protected Area, the Angkor Heritage Site, the Siem Reap City Area, the Tonle Sap Lake Area, and the Siem Reap New Tourism Area.
At the same time, Siem Reap has been transforming into a modern heritage city with the growth of businesses that serve the tourism sector, such as hotels, restaurants, shops, etc. Meanwhile, the surrounding area is also embedded with traditions and customs that continue to adhere to daily life, coupled with the warm smiles of the Cambodian people.
In order to be able to pursue a vision of sustainable development, the master plan needs to define a common scope, including cultural and ecotourism, while currently visiting Angkor Wat is the single main reason for tourists to visit Siem Reap. The master plan is to study and identify strategies to increase the attractiveness of the entire Siem Reap area as well as the surrounding area, which is more than just visiting temples, associated with a variety of recreational activities.
In this regard, Siem Reap must strengthen its qualifications to seize the opportunities available in the international market and be ready for new challenges such as the trend of slowing global economic growth, trade wars between world powers. He and the effects of the Kovid crisis 19.
The Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035 must adhere to the principles of preserving and utilizing these cultural and natural qualities to the maximum by expanding the activities and entertainment events to increase the satisfaction and attractiveness of tourists to increase The length of stay as well as increase the cost of tourists and capture higher value from the tourism sector for the benefit of the people in Siem Reap and Cambodia.
The Head of the Royal Government requested all stakeholders to participate in tourism development activities and to have clear management mechanisms in the form of their respective tourism destination management units, accompanied by public and private investment support, as well as to provide the necessary infrastructure and coordination. Relevant ministries and institutions due to the fact that tourism is inter-sectoral.
Nearly 130 million people worldwide have been infected with Kovid 19, while nearly 3 million have died. In Cambodia, more than 2,000 people were diagnosed with Kovid 19 and 20 died (16 died of Kovid 19 and 4 died of other illnesses).
For more than a year, doctors around the world have been working to find a vaccine against 19 cases of Kovid, as each country's leaders have put in place various measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in the most difficult of circumstances. So far, every country in the world has set the highest expectations for the 19 Kovid vaccine to improve the well-being of its people and improve their social and economic processes.
Many countries compete to buy vaccines for their people. Some rich countries have bought and stockpiled vaccines, urging experts from the World Health Organization and humanitarian organizations to share vaccines equitably with poor countries that cannot afford them.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, is no different from any other country in the world, striving to overcome the difficulties caused by 19 diseases with the utmost care. In addition to addressing the impact on the national economy and the well-being of the people, the search for the Kovid 19 vaccine to inject the people is also a tough effort of the Royal Government.
Through clear planning, good foresight, and good relations with friendly countries, especially its iron friend, the Chinese superpower, Cambodia received a series of 19 Kovid vaccines, which were then given to its people. Cambodia is seen as a country that gets vaccinated at a fast pace and plans to vaccinate its people better and faster.
As of March 31, 2021, Cambodia has received more than 3 million doses of vaccine for vaccination. Of that, 1.3 million doses is a generous grant from the Chinese government to the Royal Government of Cambodia, 1.5 million doses is a vaccine that Cambodia bought from China's Sinovak for $ 15 million, and 324,000 doses is a CAVAC grant. Through the World Health Organization.
Through the presence of these vaccines, Cambodia has already vaccinated nearly 400,000 people, both armed and civilian. After receiving a series of vaccines, Samdech Techo Hun Sen prepared a plan to expedite vaccination, set up a commission for 19 Kovid vaccines and announced plans to inject 1 million doses per month.
On April 1, the Sinovak vaccination campaign, which Cambodia bought from China, began, targeting more than 740,000 people. Vaccinations are conducted at up to 109 locations across the country.
Despite the detailed and clear plan, the vaccination plan will not be successful if all people do not participate and do not go for vaccination, because the principle of vaccination is still voluntary. .
Some people are reluctant to go for vaccinations because of the loss of confidence and because of the most provocative propaganda from some people who fled the country and are considered to be haunted by the Cambodian nation. These vampires have been trying to spread unfortunate news that Chinese vaccines are a health problem and try to prevent people from getting vaccinated.
Are Vaccines as Dangerous as Demons? According to international media reports, China's two vaccines, Sinofam and Sinovak, have been distributed to about 80 countries around the world, and about 106 million Chinese people have been vaccinated.
In addition, WHO experts on March 31, 2021 also confirmed and confirmed that both Chinese vaccines are safe and effective for use against Kovid 19.
What is clear is that China's Sinofam vaccine has already been given to tens of thousands of Cambodians and they do not have any health problems.
Therefore, through this information, Cambodians can consider and weigh in on the Chinese vaccine. Should we let our health problems, our family health, our lives, our family life be cut off, be determined by a group of foreign demons?
Therefore, in order to successfully participate in the fight against Kovid 19 to improve our well-being, our family's well-being, our social well-being and return to normal, we must get the Kovid 19 vaccine. Get vaccinated against Kovid 19 and end the grief for our family and our society because of Kovid 19.
