In this introductory letter, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that "This road map shows a clear vision for the restoration and promotion of post-Kovid-19 tourism in Cambodia, indicating that Cambodia may receive approximately international tourists." "7 million at the latest by 2025 and about 11 million domestic tourists by 2023."
In this sense, Cambodia's tourism sector is ready to recover under the U-shape for international tourism and the V-shape for domestic tourism.
In the same message, it was stated that Kovid-19 has caused an unprecedented crisis and shocked Cambodia, the region and the world. The impact of Kovid-19 has led to a 80.2% drop in international tourists to Cambodia and a 20% drop in domestic tourists, with a loss of about $ 3 billion in revenue by 2020.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has issued a roadmap on plans to restore and promote Cambodia's tourism sector in and after the Kovid-19 crisis, divided into three phases:
Refers to crisis management in a new phase and to plan for tourism rehabilitation (2020-2021) because this crisis provides an opportunity for Cambodia to reconsider the system to make Cambodia's tourism sector more resilient and efficient. Sustainable for the future. At this stage, Cambodia must work together to minimize the impact of Kovid-19 infection.
In fact, the Royal Government of Cambodia, in cooperation with the private sector, has set out a number of measures to ensure that businesses survive and retain employment in the tourism sector through seven rounds of government interventions. Already and the promotion of domestic tourism movement accompanied by the introduction of "tourism safety rules".
At this stage, the public-private partnership plays an important role in participating in the Kovid-19 Infectious Disease Prevention Campaign, especially to provide safe services as a basis for the restoration of tourism because of the increase in trust and reliability. Believing in all lines of tourism production is a key priority for tourism attraction.
Reliability and reliability from the beginning of the line to the end of the line from the international gate of the country where the tourist left to the international gate in Cambodia and continue to the accommodation, food, travel, leisure activities until the return. His country is warm.
In this sense, all stakeholders in the tourism sector must continue to adhere to the rules of tourism safety and health, because "things will not go back to the original, so we have to adapt to learn to live in a new state. One is to maintain good hygiene and be careful not to neglect.
Meanwhile, in preparation for the rehabilitation of the tourism sector, the Royal Government has decided to invest in the public infrastructure to improve the road infrastructure at priority tourism poles, including 34 roads in Sihanoukville and 38 roads in Siem Reap, which will bear fruit. The height of tourist attraction from the end of 2021 is inevitable.
In order to rehabilitate Cambodia's tourism sector after the Kovid-19 crisis (2022-2023) and minimize the impact of the Kovid-19 crisis, the Royal Government will continue to provide professional training in tourism, digital skills and expertise. Recently in line with market demand after the Kovid-19 crisis and efforts to promote the prestige of Cambodia as a safe tourism destination after the Kovid-19 crisis.
Preparation for the new future (2024-2025) of Cambodia's tourism sector aims to maximize the benefits of sustainable development of Cambodia's tourism sector in a sustainable and responsible manner before the crisis by seizing the opportunity of The Kovid-19 crisis builds the future of Cambodia's tourism sector to be sustainable, quality and smart.
Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia attends the 17th ASEAN Central Bank Governors' Meeting
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, attended the 17th ASEAN Central Bank Governors' Meeting, the 7th ASEAN Finance Ministers' Meeting and the Central Bank Governors' Meeting, and related online meetings with countries. Brunei hosts the 2021 ASEAN Chairmanship.
The purpose of this meeting is to discuss:
1. Regional and global economic situation and economic recovery policy. 2: Progress and direction to strengthen ASEAN financial integration.
On the progress of ASEAN integration, the Meeting congratulated on the achievement of a number of tasks that have helped to deepen integration. ASEAN Financial Integration aims to open up regional capital flows, provide and access to financial services, develop secure regional financial markets, improve the financial environment and connect regional payment systems to support community development. ASEAN Economy.
In 2020, ASEAN member countries achieved 19 out of 28 projects to promote integration, with Cambodia scoring high in opening up capital flows and financial services after Singapore, and also leading in Regional payment system connections, such as connected to Thailand and connecting with other members such as Singapore, Malaysia and Vietnam.
In terms of the financial environment, Cambodia has also promoted the use of financial services, especially for women, who now have about 71% of the adult population access to formal financial services in line with the ASEAN target of 70% by 2020.
However, Cambodia has a lower level of human resource development than some ASEAN countries. To bridge this gap, Cambodia, as well as Vietnam, Laos, Myanmar and Brunei, receive training and share experiences from member countries with developed economies.
In order to further promote financial integration, financial environment and financial stability in line with the ASEAN Economic Community Strategic Plan 2025, the meeting approved three main tasks:
1: Policy document on capital flow management measures.
2: Preparation of protocol for the ninth package of financial services, which will expand the liberalization of some sectors, sub-sectors, especially in the field of insurance.
