Ministry of Telecommunications advises all operators not to provide internet service at lower speeds than the advertised packages
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications (MPTC) has advised all telecom operators not to supply internet services with lower speeds than the internet packages they advertise and sell to consumers.
The instructions of the Ministry of Post said that all operators must strictly abide by the telecommunications law and relevant legal documents and must study and update the plan to build antennas in response to the use of users and geographical location by providing this plan. Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia (MPC).
For those who need to apply, they must apply to NTC before the construction of the antenna station and telecommunication network in accordance with Articles 14 and 17 of the Law on Telecommunications. On the other hand, it is necessary to apply for import-export permit, supply and distribution and a certificate recognizing that the type of telecommunication equipment is in accordance with Articles 14, 15 and 16 of the Law on Telecommunications.
As for the power supply, the operator must have sufficient power and have a backup power source at each antenna station to avoid the use and installation of telecommunication equipment such as clones, old equipment or installation contrary to technical standards.
Radio frequency transmission from antenna stations is not radiation, all countries in the world have built and used antennas to provide telecommunication services like Cambodia.
According to the guidelines of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications on "Measures to increase the efficiency and quality of telecommunications services" stated that "without the antenna station, there can be no mobile service, and if it affects the health of all countries. There is no antenna station. ”
Therefore, people must not block the construction of antenna stations on the location of other owners for health reasons, because this block is a violation of the law and legal documents in force.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has recommended the use of smart phones with quality, technical standards and clear brands to connect services easily and without risking health and life. It should check its internet speed regularly to make sure that the speed is the same as the internet package purchased from the operator.
Another factor is to stop the illegal installation and use of radio and television equipment and equipment to expand mobile services.
As a telecommunications service user, you must co-operate to report incidents related to the quality of service, such as insufficient coverage, slow internet speeds, or inconveniences in making and receiving calls at various locations to service providers. Customer service of telecommunication operators through the telephone number as attached.
For more information, Telecommunications users can contact the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia at 1272 during free business hours.
Therefore, all telecom operators and the public should be informed and cooperate responsibly.
Meanwhile, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has been measuring the quality of telecommunications services in each region to identify weaknesses or issues related to service quality and put in place practical measures. In addition, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will require telecom operators to invest in the necessary infrastructure.
