Tourism is a priority sector in contributing to the socio-economic development of Cambodia. Tourism as well as other sectors have been severely affected by the Kovid-19 crisis. For Cambodia, the rehabilitation of this sector requires clear and comprehensive thinking and orientation.
The roadmap will define the vision of turning the Kovid-19 crisis into an opportunity for Cambodia's tourism reform to become a quality, safe and sustainable tourism destination by regaining the number of international tourists and boosting tourism activities in Cambodia. District.
Roadmap on the plan to rehabilitate and promote Cambodia's tourism in and after the Kovid-19 crisis was prepared by the Ministry of Tourism and approved by the National Committee for Tourism Development, the Committee on Education, Youth, Sports, Cult, Religious Affairs, Culture and Tourism of the National Assembly, relevant ministries and institutions and the private sector as well.
The tourism rehabilitation and promotion plan will be implemented in three phases, including:
The Siem Reap Tourism Master Plan 2021-2035 was prepared by the "Inter-Ministerial Commission to Study the Master Plan for Siem Reap Tourism Development" led by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission and approved and supported by The National Committee for Tourism Development is chaired by Mr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance.
The Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan aims to enable Siem Reap to regain its pride as a major tourist destination in Cambodia and in Southeast Asia in the medium and long term.
1: Development of priority tourist sites in Siem Reap
2: Development of new tourism products
3: Promoting and attracting tourists to Siem Reap
4: Strengthening the quality and sustainability of tourism development in Siem Reap
5: Environmental management in Siem Reap
6: Development of infrastructure and strengthening connections to support tourism in Siem Reap
7: Strengthening governance to support the development of tourism in Siem Reap.
The master plan sets out a total of 44 strategies, a total of 136 implementation activities for the short, medium and long term, accompanied by 20 priority action plans.
