The Ministry advises the owners of Boreys and high-rise buildings not to give exclusive rights to operators to provide telephone and internet services in their locations
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications (MPTC) has instructed Borey and high-rise building owners not to enter into exclusive contract agreements with operators to provide telephone and internet services in Borey or high-rise locations, contrary to the principles of honest, fair and legal competition. No.
This is according to the guidelines on measures to increase the efficiency and improve the quality of telecommunications services of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, which was obtained by Fresh News.
This directive aims to promote the public interest and fair and socially responsible business by increasing the efficiency of telecommunications services and improving the quality of mobile and internet services.
In addition, the Ministry of Posts has instructed Borey and high-rise building owners to set aside space for the construction of antenna stations in the Borey or to set up light poles that can be equipped with telecommunication services.
Please be informed that the Ministry of Posts has been working to complete the preparation of legal documents related to improving the quality of telecommunication services, transaction penalties and other penalties for telecom operators who do not comply with the telecommunications law, relevant legal regulations and principles of providing quality services. .
Meanwhile, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has been measuring the quality of telecommunications services in each region to identify weaknesses or issues related to service quality and put in place practical measures. In addition, the Ministry of Posts will require telecom operators to invest in the necessary infrastructure.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will cooperate with relevant institutions to coordinate more effectively. All of the above work is the most priority activity of the Ministry's telecommunications sector reform program. Gifts to Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit through Duke Dr. Try Pheap and Lok Chumteav presented to 3 pagodas in Pursat
