Donation to the three pagodas in each pagoda: rice, noodles, raw milk, pure water, orange juice, bottled water and alcohol, pork mass and 2,000,000 Riels.
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Japan has decided to provide nearly $ 1 million to Cambodia through UNICEF Cambodia to support the Kovid-19 vaccination campaign and to improve the management of the Kovid-19 cold storage system. This is according to the press release of the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on April 1, 2021.
Nearly $ 1 million provided by the Japanese government to Cambodia is part of a package of nearly $ 36.9 million that Japan has provided to UNICEF in East Asia and the Pacific to improve the management of refrigeration systems for vaccines in 12 countries. Affected by Kovid-19 disease.
According to the press release, nearly $ 1 million of the total budget will be used to support the Royal Government of Cambodia in its efforts to vaccinate Kovid-19, especially to increase the capacity of the cooling system through the provision of infrastructure. Transportation and training of health workers.
The capacity of the refrigeration system is critical for the transport of vaccines stored at cold temperatures to maintain efficiency, including the Kovid-19 vaccine.
