Police crack down on Chinese smugglers fleeing from Chattalysak in Sihanoukville to Phnom Penh, arresting four Chinese and two Cambodians
There were five people in the car, including two Cambodian men and four Chinese men in disguised uniforms working as expressway crews, and they were taken to the Sihanoukville Provincial Police for further investigation. .
According to a report from the Sihanoukville Provincial Police, as a result of the interrogation, a Cambodian man, the driver of the car, admitted that he had followed the orders of another Cambodian man. After questioning, the police conducted a thorough search until they arrested a Cambodian man who was the mastermind and brought him to the Sihanoukville Provincial Police to continue the procedure.
After questioning the suspect, a Cambodian man whose mastermind confessed that he had transported a Chinese national from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville three times:
The four Chinese suspects confessed that they had already done so, but did not have any documents attached, and that they intended to go to Phnom Penh and continue to return to China. In this case, the Governor of Sihanoukville, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, ordered to build a case to send the two Cambodians to court, and for the Chinese to arrange the deportation from Cambodia. However, all six of them were sent for samples to find 19 Kovid.
