(Phnom Penh): In the spirit of steel friendship and helping each other in those difficult times, on Wednesday night, March 31, 2021, Kovid 19 Sinofam 700,000 doses, a sincere aid of the Chinese government, was handed over to Cambodia. Already at Phnom Penh International Airport.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, receives the vaccine, while Wang Vinthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, on behalf of the Chinese government, has already handed over the vaccine.
Kovid 19 Sinofam 700 doses is the second such donation in addition to the first 600,000 doses delivered to Cambodia on February 7. In both cases, Cambodia received 1.3 million doses of Chinese vaccine.
Cambodia, like the rest of the world, is suffering from Kovid 19. So far, Cambodia has identified 19 cases of Kovid 19 and 1340 cases of the disease.
In addition to health measures to prevent the spread of the disease, Kovid 19 vaccine is a method and expectation for Cambodia to improve the social, economic and living conditions of its people. Therefore, the vaccine that the Chinese government provides for Cambodia is an invaluable aid.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, considers vaccination to be one of the main strategies for Cambodia in the fight against Kovid 19. Samdech Techo called that the succession of vaccinations after the Chinese government was due to the good relations between Cambodia and China, which were started by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk and are now being raised by Samdech Techo himself.
Kovid 19 vaccine is the most in-demand product. China is also in high demand to vaccinate its people, however, the Chinese government has been reluctant to provide vaccines to Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen once claimed that without good relations, Cambodia would not have received the Kovid 19 vaccine from the Chinese government during this difficult time.
The Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of China have been seen as stepping up cooperation in the fight against Kovid 19 since the outbreak in late 2019. Wang Winthean, a representative of the Chinese government, has stated that the Chinese government will continue to cooperate with the Royal Government of Cambodia and support until Cambodia overcomes Kovid 19.
With the help of 700,000 doses of vaccine plus 1.5 million doses of Sinovak vaccine purchased at a special price from a Chinese company, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced plans to expedite vaccination to the people. Samdech Techo announced to use 1 month to vaccinate 1 million doses.
Through a series of immunization plans and access to vaccines, it is expected that Cambodia will be able to overcome Kovid 19 and improve the social, economic and living conditions of its people.
It should be noted that up to now, Cambodia has three types of vaccines to be given to the people, including: Sinofam vaccine with the help of the Chinese government, Sinovak vaccine purchased from a Chinese company and AstraZenica vaccine with Kovak assistance through the World Health Organization. Visit the gallery of international events on March 31, 2021 (Photo inside)
