(Phnom Penh): The top 10 short videos were selected and released on March 30, 2021 yesterday after the closing ceremony last weekend by the local French Higher Education Agency (AUF). Phnom Penh. While three videos were ranked as the best of the 10 short videos.
Following the announcement, many commentators expressed their enthusiasm, support and quick sharing on social media of the results, which were eagerly awaited by young contestants and French-speaking fans of Higher education institutions use French in Cambodia.
Three of the top 10 short videos are the work of student Chhorn Tola (1st place winner from the Institute of Technology of Cambodia).
Second: Student Ros Reaksa (2nd place winner from Royal University of Law and Economics) and Hang Sonimit student (3rd place winner from Institute of Technology of Cambodia).
And 3: The three students who received the incentive award were Chamroeun Puth Vichheka (from the Royal School of Law and Economics), Thorn Srey Leak (from the Royal University of Phnom Penh) and Nou Sopharith (from the University). Royal High School of Agriculture, Chamkar Dong).
Three students from the Royal University of Law and Economics and one from the University of Health Sciences will receive an award from the French Agency for Higher Education (AUF).
The purpose of this second short video game focuses on the theme: "My life as a student during the Kovit-19 epidemic is to make young people express their experiences, difficulties and studies during "The spread of Kovit-19 will promote the use of French through digital tools and youth creativity."
Please be reminded that due to the outbreak of Kovid-19, almost all Francophone activities and events have been postponed or canceled in Cambodia, as well as in cities and other countries that share the French language together in the world.
(Phnom Penh): Since Cambodia experienced the Kovid-19 crisis, Chipmung has been actively involved with the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against the epidemic.
On March 19, 2020, Chip Mong donated US $ 500,000 to the Royal Government of Cambodia for activities to prevent and control the Kovid-19 epidemic. On December 7, 2020, Chip Mong donated US $ 3 million to the Royal Government to purchase the free Kovid-19 vaccine for free.
On February 24, 2021, Chip Mong donated 5 million masks to the Royal Government of Cambodia, just days after the February 20 community event. On March 11, 2021, Chip Mong decided to donate an additional US $ 3 million to the Royal Government to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease at the February 20 community event.
Meanwhile, Khmer Breweries, one of Chip Mong's commercials, has transformed billboards across the country and digitally into educational broadcasts of "Measures: 3, 3, 3" at a cost of more than 150,000. Dollars. Khmer Breweries also donated tens of thousands of cases of Cambodian pure water and soft drinks to police officers at the Charity Hospital and the Kovid-19 Vaccination Hospital under the "Cambodian Motivation" campaign.
Chip Mong always contributes to the Royal Government of Cambodia on time and under all circumstances, especially in the campaign against Kovid-19 to participate in the development of Cambodia.
