(Stung Treng): Forces from the Anti-Drug Bureau of Stung Treng Provincial Police arrested a Lao transnational drug trafficker with nearly 3 kilograms of drugs at the second point of the corridor (Cambodia Waterway - Laos) in the village / commune of Ou Svay district, Stung Treng province at 10:30 on March 31, 2021.
The operation, led by Lt. Col. Cham Phanit, director of the Stung Treng Provincial Police Anti-Drug Bureau, said the operation to crack down on drug distribution was under the direction of Lt. Col. Phay Raksmey, deputy police chief. Stung Treng province receives anti-drug crime plan.
Lt. Col. Phay Raksmey said that the operation arrested a suspect named Pet Samon Noy, a 29-year-old Lao man living in Hat Say Khun village, Champasak province, Laos and confiscated drug exhibits. Three large packages weigh 2,990.2 grams.
The Colonel continued that after detaining the suspects, the specialized office force sent the suspects and exhibits to the Stung Treng Provincial Police to build a case to be sent to court for legal proceedings. Defamation of Xinjiang's cotton products is a human rights joke
BEIJING (Xinhua) - China's Xinjiang region has recently become a major target of Western opposition forces for painting China. From the words "genocide" to "forced labor", Western anti-Chinese forces have tried their best to spread all kinds of lies related to the Xinjiang issue.
In fact, recalling some of the lies about Xijiang fabricated by the United States and the West in recent years, as well as the so-called "sanctions" on China made by Based on these lies, it can be seen that the use of Xinjiang cotton in connection with "forced labor" is still a well-known rumor-making act.
Relevant multinational enterprises should think clearly and intelligently about this issue. Anyone who chooses to believe a lie will pay a heavy price. Those who paid the price were not anti-Chinese politicians, but multinationals who chose to become "chess pieces" of the anti-Chinese forces. Their payment is likely to lose the Chinese market.
Over the past year, China's total annual exports and imports have broken new records, while international markets have broken records, becoming the world's only major economic entity. Achieved positive growth of commodity trade. The largest trading partners of more than 120 countries and regions, including the United States, the European Union, Japan and India, are all China.
