Koh Kong Provincial Authorities Dismantle 62 Cottages and Divisions of Illegal Land in Khemarak Phoumin City
(Koh Kong): Koh Kong Provincial Unity Command led by Mr. Sok Sothy, Deputy Governor and coordinated by Mr. Wai Phirom, Deputy Prosecutor of the Provincial Court and Mr. Chheng Sovannda, Governor of the Royal Khemarak Municipality, led a joint force to dismantle the slums and blockade State at the eastern point of the airport in Boeung Khun Chhang village, Sangkat Smach Meanchey, Khemarak Phoumin city, Koh Kong province on March 31, 2021.
Mr. Sok Sothy said, "The land that the criminals stole was divided into lots with 62 plots and the huts and fences were divided into 62 private plots of land, which are state roads." For public development, today, the provincial and municipal command forces dismantled all the huts and fences, and the municipal and local authorities will search for brokers to have legal procedures.
