Khmer Breweries donates Cambodian fresh water to 4 more health centers for distribution to vaccinated seniors
(Phnom Penh): Khmer Breweries on March 30, 2021 donated another 400 cases of Cambodian pure water to Samaki Health Center, Boeung Thom Health Center, Prey Veng Health Center and Stung Meanchey Health Center in Phnom Penh for doctors to drink and distribute. To people who go to get the Kovid-19 vaccine.
Dr. Im Sothearith, Director of Public Relations, Khmer Breweries, said that the donation was part of the "Cambodian Motivation" campaign, which is actively working to donate clean water to institutions, especially hospitals and police inspectors. Mission to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 virus.
Ms. Veng Sambol, Director of Samaki Health Center, also said that her hospital could not afford to buy pure water for those who come to receive services at this hospital. However, the donation of pure water from Khmer Breweries gives her hospital the opportunity to provide better services by having fresh water distributed to Cambodians while waiting to be vaccinated.
For two days, March 29 and 30, 2021, Khmer Breweries sponsored 8 out of 13 hospitals in 14 districts of Phnom Penh. The company will continue to distribute to 5 more hospitals in the future.
Please be informed that Khmer Breweries Company was established by Chip Mong Company, one of the leading companies in Cambodia, investing in many fields. Khmer Breweries produces Cambodian beer, Kudo beer, energy drink, orange juice, ice and Cambodian pure water, which are all very popular products in the market.
Section 52 of National Road No. 5 splits from National Road No. 5 to the foot of Kampong Chhnuk Trou, Kampong Chhnang Province.
(Kampong Chhnang): The section of Road No. 52 from the beginning of Chreng down to the mouth of Chhnuk Trou canal is located in Chhnuk Trou village, Chhnuk Trou commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province, with a length of 2,700 meters. Rubber and concrete. This was confirmed by Chhnuk Trou commune authorities on the morning of March 31, 2021.
Mr. Saing Kimsorn, Chief of Chhnuk Trou Commune, said that the 2,700-meter-long section of Road 52 from the original point down to the mouth of the canal has been rebuilt by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to become a paved road and a paved road. Concrete under construction by the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kampong Chhnang Province.
The commune chief confirmed that the road, which was rebuilt by raising it one meter higher than the old road, was 2,700 meters long. Of that, 2,200 meters will be paved and the remaining 500 meters will be paved with concrete, because this 500-meter road is next to the water for fear of collapsing.
