General knowledge: Which country gives women the right to vote first and last?
(World): Getting the right to vote that we have today may be a simple thing for some people, but looking back at history, getting the right to vote is very important for the general population. For women only. Do you know which country gave women the right to vote first and last so far?
In Europe, Northern European countries are leading the way in women's suffrage, with Finland first allowing women to vote in 1906, followed by Norway, Denmark, Iceland and the United States. Sweden, which was implemented between 1913-1921. In Azerbaijan, women were allowed to vote in 1918.
Following the Nordic countries, other European countries also focused on this, with post-World War I countries Austria, Germany, Britain, Poland and Russia giving women the right to vote. In 1918, the Netherlands (1981) applied in 1981, while Spain did the same in 1931.
