Two people died immediately at the scene after a motorcycle hit a cow and fell under a truck in Suong City, Tbong Khmum Province
(Tbong Khmum): A horrific traffic accident occurred when a motorbike hit a cow that was crossing the road, causing two rear riders to fall under the car, crushing the brain and killing him immediately at the scene. The motorcyclist was injured and the car fled.
The accident happened this morning, March 31, 2021, on National Road 7 in Pun Reay village, Suong commune, Suong city, Tbong Khmum province.
According to a source from the Suong traffic police, the victim was a black Wave Shark motorbike without a license plate driven by Dum Mao, a 47-year-old Cambodian man living in Pur Ty village, Pur Ty commune, Sithor Kandal district, Prey Veng province. The cow caused two people to ride in the back of the truck and died on the spot.
The two who died were: Yim Nan, a 65-year-old Khmer woman from Po Ty village, Po Ty commune, Sithor Kandal district, Prey Veng province, was the mother-in-law of Dum Mao, and the other was Phnouk Phnong, a 13-year-old Khmer girl from the village. Together.
Currently, the authorities are making measurement records to deal with according to legal procedures, the injured were sent to the hospital, and the body was sent to the traditional ceremony in the hometown.
