Sous Yara: Cultural diplomacy is a way for peace and prosperity
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sous Yara, Director General of the Asian Cultural Council (ACC), on March 30, 2021, participated as an honorary speaker in an online seminar on "Peaceful Unification of the Korean Peninsula: Educational Perspectives and Culture." »Of the Northeast Asia Initiative 2021-2023, organized by the Global Peace Federation (UPF) in the Asia-Pacific region.
The purpose of the Initiative for Peace is to contribute to the unification of the Korean Peninsula through the participation of experts from the public sector, academics, researchers and civil society, especially through personal contacts seeking ways to change The conflict stalled towards respectful relations, cooperation and reconciliation between the two governments and peoples of Korea.
On this occasion, Mr. Sous Yara mentioned that cultural diplomacy is a way to achieve a peaceful Korean Peninsula, requiring patience and the start of planting cultural seeds, which can take 10 to 50 years to tree. Grows and bears fruit.
"Culture creates a bridge of dialogue and building trust between countries and the region," he said. "Cultural diplomacy is a way for peace and prosperity."
