The Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation is the first credit guarantee company in Cambodia to be established by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, as a public enterprise under the technical and financial guardianship of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. The main mission of the Cambodian Credit Assurance Corporation is to provide credit guarantees to participating financial institutions (PFIs) to support businesses that are able to repay but lack collateral when applying for a loan.
The first package of the Business Recovery Credit Scheme (BRGS) will contribute $ 200 million in new credit in the banking sector for businesses applying for loans from participating financial institutions (PFIs) of the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation, including ACLEDA Bank, Institutions. AMK Microfinance, Asia Pacific Development Bank, Cambodia Post Bank, Canadia Bank, Phillip Bank and Prince Bank.
The loan guarantee scheme will be provided to a number of banks and other microfinance institutions that are preparing to become participating financial institutions (PFIs) of the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation. The credit guarantee of the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation will act as collateral from 70% to 80% of the amount of credit provided by participating financial institutions (PFIs), thus reducing the demand for collateral from businesses applying for a loan.
He called on banks and microfinance institutions to support the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation through participation as participatory financial institutions (PFIs) and strengthen credit governance.
The Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation welcome close cooperation with all relevant institutions to support business development through the BRGS.
