(World): After seceding from the British colony, the United States officially declared independence on July 4, 1776, when the new federal state had only 13 states. Do you know which country was the first to declare US independence?
The Kingdom of Morocco was the first country to declare US independence. Morocco is an ancient kingdom with a history dating back to the 8th century BC, now located in northwestern Africa and bordering Spain and Portugal.
In 1786, Morocco officially recognized the independence of the United States and signed a peace treaty with the United States, which is considered to be the longest document in US history.
Since 1905, diplomatic relations between the two countries have also improved.
Morocco came under French protection from 1912-1956, and when Morocco liberated from the French protectorate in 1956, the United States was the first country to recognize Morocco independence and maintain good relations until Currently.
In 2004, the United States formed a steel alliance with Morocco, and the two armies frequently conducted joint exercises and exercises to strengthen regional and global security, even though Morocco is not a NATO member. By (Non-NATO).
Morocco is now a strong partner of the United States in counter-terrorism efforts to protect each other's national security interests. Chef Kakada Sophorn who went to Takeo province was found to be positive for Kovid 19 after the third test
