On March 28, 2021, Mr. Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Justice, reminded of the sanctions in Sub-Decree No. 37 on "Disposal of Kovid 19-infected bodies" in violation of this sub-decree. He said that in cases where there is a suspicion that the body may be infected with Kovid-19 virus, the family must cooperate with health officials to take samples from the body to be tested for Kovid-19 virus.
While waiting for the results of the autopsy, the body shall be under the temporary control of the Ministry of Health in cooperation with the competent authorities. In the event that the results of the analysis confirm that the corpse is not infected with Kovid-19 virus, the Ministry of Health must hand over the corpse to the corpse family for further management and disposal.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sim Sitha, Director General of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, expects that the revenue of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority in 2021 will continue to increase as planned, while in 2020 earn more than 79 Million dollars, an increase of about 50 percent.
Mr. Sim Sitha stated that "the revenue in 2020 of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has increased and we expect in 2021 also increase, but not much."
Mr. Sim Sitha said that the water price of the Water Supply Authority has changed due to the subsidy for people who use less than 7 or 10 cubic meters, with cheaper sales than the original price. He said that in the case of growing businesses, the price of water will also increase, but when ordinary customers come to use more water, the price of water will be reduced and revenue will also decrease.
The Director General of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority confirmed that the Water Supply Authority of Phnom Penh needs to be weighed and not fully assessed and managed due to the main problem of water loss, because losing water is like losing money, and water is An important skill. That is why the team is working to increase the efficiency of water management to prevent water loss.
