According to Touch Chhay, executive director of the Kampong Cham Red Cross branch, Khem Nary was a former Koh Sotin district women's affairs officer since 1979 and resigned in 1986. He has three sons and daughters, but his family has moved to another place, leaving him alone in a small, dilapidated hut.
On the other hand, in addition to the state subsidy provided through two vouchers, he earns only 1,000 to 2,000 riel a day, and his livelihood depends only on the kindness of his neighbors.
Mr. Touch Chhay continued that after learning about the difficult situation of the poor woman, the Chairman of the Branch Committee, Mr. Un Chanda, decided to provide a house 4 meters by 6 meters high, with a construction cost of more than 9 million. Riel for him to stay forever.
Please note that the humanitarian donations provided to Ms. Khem Nary for the new house include: 75 kg of rice, 10 cans of fish, 6 bottles of fish sauce, 6 bottles of soy sauce, 1 box of noodles, 1 kit, 2 T-shirts , Sleeping equipment, some kitchen equipment and a budget of 200,000 riels. Separately, 13 more needy families received donations in each family, including rice, fish, noodles, fish sauce, soy sauce and T-shirt, as well as a budget of 20,000 riels.
