Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Introduces Fines for Those Who Do Not Apply Masks and Gaps (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior Work closely with health officials to enforce transactional fines on individuals or legal entities that do not perform their obligations to wear masks and to maintain personal safety.
The recommendation of Samdech Krala Hom was made through a letter sent to the Capital-Provincial Governor on March 27, 2021.
Please be reminded that on March 24, 2021, the Ministry of Health decided to designate Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville, Kandal, Prey Veng and Siem Reap as Kovid-19 outbreaks in the required February 20 community event. To carry out the duty of wearing a mask and the duty to maintain a safety gap.
According to the sub-decree on health measures to prevent the transmission of Kovid 19, it is determined that those who do not comply with the obligation to wear masks and maintain personal safety gaps will be fined from 200,000 to 1 million riels.
