Xi Jinping Leads to Victory in Poverty Eradication: Part 10! Final Victory
(Beijing): In the long history of the world, poverty has always been one of the most complex challenges facing humanity. New China has entered a new era capable of fighting poverty. But the path to eradicating poverty is not smooth, as China's path to poverty reduction is full of great flexibility.
Under the direct leadership of Chinese President Xi Jinping, poverty reduction measures have been implemented effectively. By the end of 2020, nearly 100 million rural poor people will be lifted out of poverty, 832 poor districts will be eradicated, absolute poverty will be eradicated, the fight against poverty will be won.
Xi Jinping pointed out that the key indicators of overcoming the poverty eradication campaign by 2020 are to achieve the following goals: the poor have no worries about food and clothing, and access to education. Compulsory education, basic health care and housing safety are guaranteed.
To date, villages across China have concrete roads, each village has clinics and village doctors, 108,000 poor school facilities have been improved, and electricity supply rates have improved. In rural areas, 99% of the population has access to the internet, and in the poorest villages, 98% of the population has been lifted out of poverty.
As the world's largest developing country, China's achievements in reducing poverty have attracted the attention of the world, not just the political superiority of the Chinese Communist Party and the socialist regime. No, it has also brought confidence in poverty reduction to other countries in the world, as well as accelerated the process of global poverty reduction and received widespread praise.
UN Secretary-General Guterres says China's development has lifted hundreds of millions of people out of poverty, and China is working to eradicate the worst poverty in the country by 2020. So this is China's biggest contribution to the world.
Today, China has solved the problem of the poorest and the building of a society where the people are relatively prosperous in all respects, the Chinese Millennium Dream will be achieved in the hands of this generation.
Interior Ministry spokesman: 55 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses
(Phnom Penh): At least 55 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on March 26, 2021 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News this morning, March 27.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 55 suspects, 34 were arrested in 15 criminal cases and 21 were arrested in 12 drug cases.
