Banteay Srei District Authority Closes Two Noodle Shops in Preah Dak and Calls on Stakeholders
(Siem Reap): Banteay Srei District Governor Khim Finang wrote an urgent message on the night of March 26, 2021, calling on all people who used to eat or contact with two noodle stalls in Preah Dak village to put up People who are isolated and have symptoms such as fever, cough, sneezing, sore throat, runny nose, fatigue or shortness of breath should be screened for Kovid 19.
The announcement came after authorities closed two noodle stalls in Preah Dak village, where a 19-year-old Kovid man in Siem Reap had gone to eat before doctors found Kovid 19 positive on March 25.
Mr. Khim Finang wrote: "As an urgent measure, the district administration immediately summoned the families of the two stalls and arranged for samples from all stakeholders." "But as the situation is fragile and evolving rapidly, especially after the case passed from this positive man to the staff of a cafe in Siem Reap, which he had already entered during the same period."
The district governor continued to call on all people who used to eat or have contact with the two noodle stalls from the 19th to the 24th of March to be isolated and if there are no symptoms. Symptoms such as fever, cough, sneezing, sore throat, runny nose, fatigue or difficulty breathing must be tested at the provincial pedagogical school.
Mr. Khim Finang expressed the hope that all citizens will be honest with the authorities, help spread the word and participate in cutting off transmission in the community as soon as possible.
